{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:31:19.920Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5b9c47ec508191938d900d218f5817","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ne9NVbOs4esjY88uPu79PziF","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,260p' competitive-eval/agentic-repair-pilot/README.md && sed -n '1,220p' competitive-eval/tools/construct_oracle_agentic_overlay.py\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":24000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:31:20.110Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f75da-79ae-7ad3-ab16-c1606dd4955a","call_id":"call_ne9NVbOs4esjY88uPu79PziF","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Graph Agentic Repair Pilot\n\nThis is a development-only, three-repository repair pilot. It measures how one\nfixed coding agent uses three native repository-discovery treatments while the\nrest of the repair loop remains available:\n\n- `file-tools`: Claude Code `Read`, `Grep`, and `Glob`;\n- `entire-graph`: compact agent-format `entire-graph search` calls plus targeted reads;\n- `cbm`: the complete Codebase Memory MCP tool surface plus targeted reads.\n\nEvery arm may edit files and run tests. The checkout contains only the public\nbase commit. The agent process is sandboxed away from the controller corpus,\nfuture Git objects, sibling arms, other user repositories, and prior temporary\nruns. The issue prompt is the same hash-verified, pre-selection public title and\nbody across treatments. Treatment-specific instructions describe only which\nretrieval surface is available.\n\nThis pilot is deliberately separate from Graph V8. It does not authorize V8\ncatalog construction, ranking, scoring, publication, or a product claim. It\nreuses three cases from the already-excluded development cohort and therefore\ncannot produce confirmatory evidence.\n\n## Why this exists\n\nThe Graph V8 retrieval smoke is a deterministic component test. It invokes each\nretriever once and scores ranked source locations. That is useful for regression\ndiagnosis, but it does not reproduce an agent's iterative workflow. This pilot\nadds the missing loop: formulate searches, inspect results, read files, edit,\nrun tests, and revise.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- One pinned model and prompt are used for every arm.\n- Product and agent versions are recorded before execution.\n- Each arm receives an isolated checkout at the same base tree.\n- Future fix commits, tests, and judgments are inaccessible while any agent is running.\n- Network use and Git-history inspection are forbidden by the prompt and\n  audited from tool calls.\n- Graph and CBM use is required. Normal follow-up `Grep`, `Glob`, `Read`, and\n  shell inspection remain available so the treatment matches real coding-agent\n  use; every retrieval and shell call is recorded.\n- The file-tools arm has no Graph or CBM server.\n- Raw transcripts, patches, usage, tool calls, and validation results are\n  retained under a new run directory.\n- Missing token accounting, missing tests, treatment violations, and timeouts\n  remain visible; they are never silently excluded.\n\n## Metrics and claim boundary\n\nThe runner reports:\n\n- non-empty and syntactically clean patch rates;\n- reference file and old-side region overlap as diagnostic repair alignment;\n- agent-executed test calls and their observed tool outcomes;\n- treatment compliance;\n- model tokens, turns, tool calls, wall time, and reported cost.\n\nReference overlap and agent-selected passing tests are not task correctness. A\ndifferent correct repair can have low overlap, and a wrong repair can touch the\nreference files and pass existing tests. The runner calls that diagnostic\ncombination `observed_workflow_completion`.\n\nAfter all nine agent processes exit, the controller copies each patched checkout,\noverlays only predeclared test files from the bound future fix, and runs the\npredeclared acceptance commands. Future source hunks are never applied. The\nresult is reported separately as raw patch acceptance. The comparison metric,\n`controller_acceptance`, additionally requires that the corresponding agent\nattempt used its assigned treatment, did not time out, and exited successfully.\nFull upstream acceptance remains outside the claim boundary.\n\n## Usage\n\nThe live run is paid and must be explicitly authorized by the owner.\n\n```sh\npython3 competitive-eval/tools/run_graph_agentic_repair_pilot.py all \\\n  --output /private/tmp/graph-agentic-repair-pilot-run \\\n  --repository-catalog /absolute/path/to/sem-development-pilot-corpus/repository-catalog.json \\\n  --public-capture-catalog /absolute/path/to/sem-development-pilot-corpus/raw/github-metadata-capture-v2/capture-catalog.json \\\n  --claude-binary /absolute/path/to/claude \\\n  --graph-binary /absolute/path/to/entire-graph \\\n  --cbm-binary /absolute/path/to/codebase-memory-mcp \\\n  --model opus \\\n  --max-budget-usd 5 \\\n  --max-turns 80 \\\n  --runtime-path-prefix /path/to/node22/bin:/path/to/package-managers \\\n  --bootstrap-dependencies \\\n  --workers 3\n```\n\nLocked JavaScript dependencies are installed once by the controller, outside\nagent timing, and the exact prepared tree is copy-on-write cloned to all three\ntreatments. The bootstrap cost and tool hashes are retained separately. Agents\ncannot use network commands during repair.\n\nIf all nine immutable agent records were captured but controller acceptance\nwas interrupted, resume only the unpaid acceptance phase with the same runtime\narguments and `accept` in place of `run`. The command requires all nine unique\nrecords and does not invoke an agent.\n\nCatch2 controller runs hash-record one exact compatibility adjustment that\nexcludes an unrelated, pre-existing template-product self-test rejected by the\nhost's Apple Clang 21. The adjustment is applied identically after the bound\nfuture-test overlay for base, reference, and all three candidate patches; the\nthree issue-specific `[checked-if]` tests remain byte-identical to the public\nfix.\n\nVite controller runs build the local `vite` workspace bundle before Vitest so\nthe already-installed workspace dependency resolves from the isolated copied\ncheckout. This is an unpaid prerequisite build, not agent work.\n\nThe product treatments add Entire Graph or CBM to the same normal file and\nshell tools available to the baseline. Product use is required and recorded,\nbut follow-up Grep, Glob, Read, or shell inspection remains available. This\nmatches how coding agents use an additional retrieval product in practice.\n\nFor an unpaid harness check:\n\n```sh\npython3 -m pytest -q \\\n  competitive-eval/tools/test_run_graph_agentic_repair_pilot.py\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Freeze a compiler-oracle agentic overlay from predefined Fidelity repos.\n\nThe constructor exports each pinned Git tree to a temporary directory before\nrunning its language oracle. Focus selection uses only oracle topology and\nstable source identity; it never reads product output or benchmark scores.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nimport tarfile\nimport tempfile\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport sem_v7_artifacts as artifacts\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nDEFAULT_CORPUS = ROOT / \"corpus\"\nDEFAULT_OUTPUT = ROOT / \"competitive-eval\" / \"oracle-agentic-overlay\" / \"manifest.json\"\nSUITE = \"entire_graph_oracle_agentic_overlay_v1\"\nSELECTION_SALT = \"oracle-agentic-overlay-v1\"\nREPOSITORIES = (\n    {\"language\": \"go\", \"name\": \"chi\", \"manifest\": \"repos.json\"},\n    {\"language\": \"typescript\", \"name\": \"zod\", \"manifest\": \"repos-ts.json\"},\n    {\"language\": \"python\", \"name\": \"click\", \"manifest\": \"repos-py.json\"},\n)\n\n\nclass OverlayError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an oracle or predefined repository violates the contract.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef run(command: list[str], *, cwd: Path | None = None) -> bytes:\n    try:\n        return subprocess.run(command, cwd=cwd, check=True, capture_output=True).stdout\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as exc:\n        detail = exc.stderr.decode(errors=\"replace\").strip()\n        raise OverlayError(f\"command failed: {' '.join(command)}\\n{detail}\") from exc\n\n\ndef sha256_bytes(value: bytes) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(value).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef git_value(repo: Path, *args: str) -> str:\n    return run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(repo), *args]).decode().strip()\n\n\ndef load_repo_spec(root: Path, manifest_name: str, repo_name: str) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], Path]:\n    path = root / manifest_name\n    manifest = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    matches = [row for row in manifest.get(\"repos\", []) if row.get(\"name\") == repo_name]\n    if len(matches) != 1:\n        raise OverlayError(f\"expected one {repo_name!r} entry in {path}\")\n    return matches[0], path\n\n\ndef export_head(repo: Path, destination: Path, expected_ref: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    commit = git_value(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    ref_commit = git_value(repo, \"rev-parse\", f\"{expected_ref}^{{commit}}\")\n    if commit != ref_commit:\n        raise OverlayError(\n            f\"{repo} HEAD {commit} does not match predefined ref {expected_ref} ({ref_commit})\"\n        )\n    tree = git_value(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD^{tree}\")\n    archive = run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(repo), \"archive\", \"--format=tar\", \"HEAD\"])\n    tar_path = destination.parent / f\"{destination.name}.tar\"\n    tar_path.write_bytes(archive)\n    destination.mkdir()\n    with tarfile.open(tar_path) as bundle:\n        bundle.extractall(destination, filter=\"data\")\n    return commit, tree\n\n\ndef location(row: dict[str, Any]) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    try:\n        return str(row[\"file\"]), int(row[\"line\"])\n    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError) as exc:\n        raise OverlayError(f\"malformed oracle location: {row!r}\") from exc\n\n\ndef public_symbol(row: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"file\": str(row[\"file\"]),\n        \"line\": int(row[\"line\"]),\n        \"name\": str(row[\"name\"]),\n        \"kind\": str(row[\"kind\"]),\n    }\n\n\ndef selection_digest(language: str, symbol: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    value = (\n        f\"{SELECTION_SALT}\\0{language}\\0{symbol['file']}\\0{symbol['line']}\"\n    ).encode()\n    return sha256_bytes(value)\n\n\ndef normalize_oracle(oracle: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Remove ephemeral paths and canonicalize unordered oracle record sets.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(oracle)\n    normalized[\"repo\"] = \".\"\n    for key in (\"compiled_files\", \"symbols\", \"calls\", \"naive_calls\"):\n        if isinstance(normalized.get(key), list):\n            normalized[key] = sorted(\n                normalized[key],\n                key=lambda row: json.dumps(row, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\")),\n            )\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef select_focus(language: str, oracle: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    stats = oracle.get(\"stats\", {})\n    if stats.get(\"load_errors\") != 0:\n        raise OverlayError(f\"{language} oracle reported load errors: {stats.get('load_errors')!r}\")\n\n    symbols = {location(row): public_symbol(row) for row in oracle.get(\"symbols\", [])}\n    name_counts: dict[str, int] = defaultdict(int)\n    for symbol in symbols.values():\n        name_counts[symbol[\"name\"]] += 1\n    inbound: dict[tuple[str, int], set[tuple[str, int]]] = defaultdict(set)\n    outbound: dict[tuple[str, int], set[tuple[str, int]]] = defaultdict(set)\n    for call in oracle.get(\"calls\", []):\n        source = (str(call.get(\"from_file\")), int(call.get(\"from_line\", 0)))\n        target = (str(call.get(\"to_file\")), int(call.get(\"to_line\", 0)))\n        if source in symbols and target in symbols and source != target:\n            outbound[source].add(target)\n            inbound[target].add(source)\n\n    candidates = []\n    for key, symbol in symbols.items():\n        if name_counts[symbol[\"name\"]] != 1:\n            continue\n        callers = inbound[key]\n        callees = outbound[key]\n        if not (1 <= len(callers) <= 8 and 1 <= len(callees) <= 8):\n            continue\n        if len(callers) + len(callees) < 4 or len(callers) * len(callees) > 32:\n            continue\n        candidates.append((selection_digest(language, symbol), key))\n    if not candidates:\n        raise OverlayError(f\"no eligible focus symbol for {language}\")\n\n    digest, key = min(candidates)\n    callers = [symbols[item] for item in sorted(inbound[key])]\n    callees = [symbols[item] for item in sorted(outbound[key])]\n    focus = symbols[key]\n    return {\n        \"selection_digest\": digest,\n        \"focus\": focus,\n        \"complete_inbound\": callers,\n        \"complete_outbound\": callees,\n        \"complete_two_hop_path_count\": len(callers) * len(callees),\n        \"complete_two_hop_path_families\": [\n            {\"callers\": callers, \"focus\": focus, \"callees\": callees}\n        ],\n    }\n\n\ndef cases(repository: str, language: str, selected: dict[str, Any]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    focus = selected[\"focus\"]\n    prefix = f\"oracle-{language}-{repository}\"\n    return [\n        {\n            \"id\": f\"{prefix}-definition\",\n            \"category\": \"symbol_discovery\",\n            \"question\": f\"Locate the definition of {focus['name']}.\",\n            \"expected\": [focus],\n        },\n        {\n            \"id\": f\"{prefix}-inbound\",\n            \"category\": \"direct_callers\",\n            \"question\": f\"List every compiler-resolved direct caller of {focus['name']}.\",\n            \"expected\": selected[\"complete_inbound\"],\n        },\n        {\n            \"id\": f\"{prefix}-outbound\",\n            \"category\": \"direct_callees\",\n            \"question\": f\"List every compiler-resolved direct callee of {focus['name']}.\",\n            \"expected\": selected[\"complete_outbound\"],\n        },\n        {\n            \"id\": f\"{prefix}-two-hop\",\n            \"category\": \"transitive_call_path\",\n            \"question\": f\"List every two-hop caller -> {focus['name']} -> callee path.\",\n            \"expected_path_families\": selected[\"complete_two_hop_path_families\"],\n            \"expected_path_count\": selected[\"complete_two_hop_path_count\"],\n        },\n    ]\n\n\ndef construct_entry(\n    *, language: str, spec: dict[str, Any], manifest_path: Path,\n    commit: str, tree: str, oracle: dict[str, Any], binding: dict[str, Any],\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    selected = select_focus(language, oracle)\n    repository = str(spec[\"url\"])\n    return {\n        \"repository\": repository,\n        \"name\": spec[\"name\"],\n        \"language\": language,\n        \"predefined_ref\": spec[\"ref\"],\n        \"source_path\": spec.get(\"path\", \".\"),\n        \"commit\": commit,\n        \"tree\": tree,\n        \"source_manifest\": manifest_path.name,\n        \"source_manifest_sha256\": artifacts.sha256_file(manifest_path),\n        \"oracle_binding\": binding,\n        \"oracle_output_canonical_sha256\": sha256_bytes(artifacts.canonical_bytes(oracle)),\n        \"oracle_stats\": oracle[\"stats\"],\n        \"selection\": selected,\n        \"cases\": cases(repository, language, selected),\n    }\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
