{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:48:14.094Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba03e18188191adbfdfc0ccbf2c41","status":"completed","call_id":"call_Ij6yEuAjtkRjTI3j7M9jJ8du","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/README.md\\n@@\\n-- **Agent-native output.** `--format agent` starts with auditable cache, index, preselection, query, and total latency telemetry, then emits only ranked locations, symbol names, and focused source. Tight positive budgets use compact telemetry so the top location remains useful, and the complete wire output never exceeds the requested bytes. Use `json` or `ndjson` when a program needs the full result schema, completeness, partial failures, and search diagnostics.\\n+- **Agent-native output.** `--format agent` starts with auditable cache, index, preselection, query, and total latency telemetry, then emits only ranked locations, symbol names, and focused source. When the full header would crowd out a ranked location, tight positive budgets use compact telemetry when it fits; the complete wire output never exceeds the requested bytes. Use `json` or `ndjson` when a program needs the full result schema, completeness, partial failures, and search diagnostics.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:48:14.249Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-1f04d74d-c9f0-47a9-9c55-c968093f1b83","turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/README.md\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -188,3 +188,3 @@\n - **Bounded output.** Results are budgeted to **16 KiB** of serialized snippets by default, sized to drop straight into a model context window. Tune with `--top-k` and `--max-context-bytes` (`--max-context-bytes 0` for an unbounded diagnostic ranking).\n-- **Agent-native output.** `--format agent` starts with auditable cache, index, preselection, query, and total latency telemetry, then emits only ranked locations, symbol names, and focused source. Tight positive budgets use compact telemetry so the top location remains useful, and the complete wire output never exceeds the requested bytes. Use `json` or `ndjson` when a program needs the full result schema, completeness, partial failures, and search diagnostics.\n+- **Agent-native output.** `--format agent` starts with auditable cache, index, preselection, query, and total latency telemetry, then emits only ranked locations, symbol names, and focused source. When the full header would crowd out a ranked location, tight positive budgets use compact telemetry when it fits; the complete wire output never exceeds the requested bytes. Use `json` or `ndjson` when a program needs the full result schema, completeness, partial failures, and search diagnostics.\n - **Focused regions.** Semantic results span at most 80 lines by default, keeping locations precise while snippets remain independently capped at 40 lines. Override with `--max-region-lines` and `--max-snippet-lines` when broader context is useful.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed"}}
