{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:49:32.599Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba08c9c4481918b79dc0d3a434ab7","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Product checkpoint `188180d` is now on GitHub. I’m moving to the second half of the fix: the unpaid evaluation freeze. I’ll add identity-safe HMAC disjointness, separate public questions from sealed qrels, bind the exact Graph/CBM binaries and schedule, and add preflight-only validation—without launching Claude or any paid run."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:49:32.611Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba08c9f248191b8215d4f6e44328e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_KyvsF8YcbXNS2AbFHtQhzjys","name":"exec","input":"const rs = await Promise.all([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git status --short --branch && git rev-parse HEAD && git rev-parse @{u}\",workdir:\"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:4000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"find .. -name AGENTS.md -print\",workdir:\"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:5000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null\",workdir:\"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:12000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,260p' competitive-eval/preindexed-agentic-v2/README.md\",workdir:\"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:18000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ls -la competitive-eval/preindexed-agentic-v2 && rg -n \\\"latency|telemetry|execution_config|preflight|authorization|paid\\\" competitive-eval/tools/run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py | head -160\",workdir:\"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:12000})\n]);\nfor (const r of rs) text(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:49:33.848Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f75eb-2a18-78e0-a409-856fba4a54f5","call_id":"call_KyvsF8YcbXNS2AbFHtQhzjys","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"56f58f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002917,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":40,\"output\":\"## codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot...origin/codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot\\nbcb60c7929241759b2921ead627a8e36b93b0065\\nbcb60c7929241759b2921ead627a8e36b93b0065\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"2791ec\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.002333833,\"session_id\":10953,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"c900ff\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003042,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"341b47\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":987,\"output\":\"# Preindexed Agentic Measurement Protocol\\n\\nThe completed `20260718` compiler-oracle smoke remains immutable diagnostic\\nevidence. Its transcripts, raw records, authorization, recovery record,\\nscoreboard, report, and overlay documentation are not rescored or rewritten by\\nthis protocol.\\n\\n## Historical comparison boundary\\n\\nThe historical wall-time comparison is invalid. The timed Entire Graph arm was\\nrequired to run an uncached selective `search` and a separately cached full\\n`neighbors` build. One Zod attempt also invoked `neighbors` without `--head`,\\nwhich forced another worktree build. The CBM arm was instructed to index during\\nthe task and repeatedly returned a degraded index. These setup costs were inside\\nthe agent timer and competed across concurrent attempts.\\n\\nThe historical prompt also forced Entire Graph to use `search`, then\\n`neighbors`, then file-tool verification. The file-tools arm had no comparable\\nminimum workflow. Consequently, task latency cannot be repaired by subtracting\\na single observed indexing duration.\\n\\nRaw transcript facts such as returned answers, provider token billing, and tool\\ncalls remain useful diagnostics of that exact treatment. They are not clean\\ncausal estimates for the repaired product or corrected protocol.\\n\\n## Replacement protocol\\n\\nNew runs use `preindexed-agentic-v2` and a new output directory.\\n\\n1. Materialize and verify the exact committed repository tree.\\n2. Build each product index before any paid agent process starts.\\n3. Validate the index against the exact tree, product version, binary hash,\\n   profile, and isolated cache. Entire Graph must produce a fresh miss followed\\n   by a hit with nonempty, complete counts. CBM must report the exact indexed\\n   project and nonzero nodes from a second process. Any missing, degraded,\\n   corrupt, partial, empty, or unexpected state aborts the whole run before a\\n   paid attempt launches.\\n4. Record setup/index duration separately from task duration.\\n5. Give each product arm symmetric instructions: use its assigned preindexed\\n   retrieval system as primary, choose the appropriate retrieval call, and use\\n   targeted file reads only when useful. Do not force duplicate verification.\\n6. Require timed Entire Graph search to consume the complete prepared index\\n   with `--index-all-files`, and require every Graph retrieval to use the exact\\n   validated committed-tree cache. Reject worktree builds, alternate caches,\\n   cache misses, no-cache calls, and non-retrieval Graph commands.\\n7. Reject CBM indexing, CLI use, project mutation, wrong-project retrieval, or\\n   unhealthy retrieval during a timed task.\\n8. Commit an `attempt-start.json` before every paid process, binding the prompt,\\n   command, sandbox, MCP config, setup record, and exact execution config.\\n   Resume and recovery fail closed when any binding differs.\\n9. Run both setup and paid attempts sequentially for uncontended latency.\\n   Persist an invalid transcript and record, then abort before launching another\\n   paid attempt on any treatment violation.\\n10. Report cached retrieval and end-to-end agent latency separately from setup\\n    and incremental-update cost.\\n\\nThe corrected runner refuses to write into an evidence directory whose\\nexecution configuration does not declare `preindexed-agentic-v2`, and refuses\\nto resume when an existing v2 configuration differs byte-for-byte in canonical\\ncontent. Prepare, run, recovery, and rescore share the same legacy-evidence\\nguard.\\n\\n## Claim boundary\\n\\nThe same three repositories are a development regression smoke only. They can\\nverify that diagnosed defects no longer recur, but they cannot support a broad\\nsuperiority claim after the outcomes have been observed. A claim requires a\\nfresh, outcome-blind predefined slice, frozen product and comparator heads,\\nexplicit semantics for abstract declarations, constructors, generated mirrors,\\nand repeated paired attempts.\\n\\nNo paid rerun is authorized by this protocol document.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7d69c7\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":533,\"output\":\"total 8\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 thomi  wheel    96 Jul 18 16:00 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 24 thomi  wheel   768 Jul 18 16:00 ..\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 thomi  wheel  3946 Jul 18 16:39 README.md\\n483:        raise SmokeError(f\\\"{label} failed before paid execution: {detail}\\\")\\n496:    execution_config_sha256: str, product_binding: dict[str, Any],\\n498:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Prepare and validate product state before any paid agent process starts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n623:        \\\"execution_config_sha256\\\": execution_config_sha256,\\n644:    execution_config_sha256: str, product_binding: dict[str, Any],\\n652:            execution_config_sha256=execution_config_sha256,\\n662:        or setup.get(\\\"execution_config_sha256\\\") != execution_config_sha256\\n836:        \\\"execution_config_sha256\\\": setup[\\\"execution_config_sha256\\\"],\\n879:        \\\"execution_config_sha256\\\": setup[\\\"execution_config_sha256\\\"],\\n907:    execution_config_sha256: str, model: str, max_turns: int,\\n930:        or setup.get(\\\"execution_config_sha256\\\") != execution_config_sha256\\n943:        or attempt_start.get(\\\"execution_config_sha256\\\") != execution_config_sha256\\n956:            or existing.get(\\\"execution_config_sha256\\\") != execution_config_sha256\\n1021:        \\\"execution_config_sha256\\\": execution_config_sha256,\\n1114:    execution_config_sha256 = artifacts.sha256_file(config_path)\\n1122:            or source.get(\\\"execution_config_sha256\\\") != execution_config_sha256\\n1173:        raise SmokeError(\\\"preindexed-agentic-v2 requires --workers 1 for uncontended latency measurement\\\")\\n1175:    execution_config = {\\n1196:        if previous != execution_config:\\n1200:        execution_config_sha256 = artifacts.sha256_file(existing_config)\\n1202:        execution_config_sha256 = canonical_write(existing_config, execution_config)\\n1206:        \\\"file-tools\\\": {\\\"claude\\\": execution_config[\\\"claude\\\"]},\\n1209:            \\\"binary\\\": execution_config[\\\"entire_graph\\\"],\\n1211:        \\\"cbm\\\": {\\\"binary\\\": execution_config[\\\"cbm\\\"]},\\n1214:    # Fail closed before launching any paid process. Index setup is deliberately\\n1224:                execution_config_sha256=execution_config_sha256,\\n1239:                execution_config_sha256=execution_config_sha256,\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
