{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:05:39.458Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Entire Graph’s product fixes are already committed, pushed, and green on PR #43. I’m finishing the honest three-repository issue-analysis smoke gate now: fresh protected-set exclusion, agent-visible tasks separated from sealed relevance judgments, and a runner that cannot launch while authorization is false. No paid agent run is being started.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:05:39.458Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba45374a081918fb830666df4bb1c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Entire Graph’s product fixes are already committed, pushed, and green on PR #43. I’m finishing the honest three-repository issue-analysis smoke gate now: fresh protected-set exclusion, agent-visible tasks separated from sealed relevance judgments, and a runner that cannot launch while authorization is false. No paid agent run is being started."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:05:39.458Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba45377c0819197afd5a8b0e16452","name":"list_agents","namespace":"collaboration","arguments":"{}","call_id":"call_AmQ4iHmMF3UfbGFYM2Aco2Ss","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:05:39.507Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019f75f9-e633-7612-8477-6dd626043c7c","call_id":"call_AmQ4iHmMF3UfbGFYM2Aco2Ss","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/agentic_design_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Bottom line: the repository has enough public metadata to nominate code-repair cases, but not enough committed oracle/environment data to freeze a runnable CORE-Bench/Multi-SWE actual-agent manifest today. CORE-Bench itself is a retrieval benchmark here; its qrels cannot honestly score a patch.\\n\\nKey findings:\\n\\n- The candidate catalog is repository-level metadata only: pinned CORE/Multi-SWE revisions, repo/language, and query/qrel/corpus counts. It contains no repair prompt, test command, or test artifact ([candidate-catalog.json](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/core-bench/candidate-catalog.json:1)).\\n- The spike deterministically froze eight repos × three queries before adapter work, with six repos sealed and qrels forbidden to systems ([spike-manifest.json](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/core-bench/spike-manifest.json:508), [selection](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/core-bench/spike-manifest.json:639)).\\n- Each case exposes a usable public projection: repo, language, base commit, query/PR identity, and `issue_text`; it only hashes qrels/candidate IDs ([core_bench_graph_spike.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/core_bench_graph_spike.py:489)). Some checked-in `issue_text` is plainly PR-derived implementation prose, so it may leak solution direction. Prefer the official Multi-SWE problem statement or captured original issue if that field can be extracted without reading the gold patch.\\n- The source binding intentionally records only Multi-SWE file paths and says embedded patches were not downloaded ([core_bench_graph_spike.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/core_bench_graph_spike.py:564), [spike-manifest.json](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/core-bench/spike-manifest.json:838)). The README likewise says CORE corpus documents lack paths/base commits and that gold patches were avoided ([README.md](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/core-bench/README.md:159)).\\n- CORE evaluation ranks candidate source chunks and later scores them against qrels; it never executes a patch or tests ([core_bench_graph_eval.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/core_bench_graph_eval.py:812), [qrel scoring](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/core_bench_graph_eval.py:1256)). These are retrieval questions, even though the query sounds like a development request.\\n- The current three-repo smoke is also retrieval-only: six definition/snippet/search/callgraph questions per repo ([construct_agentic_tasks_smoke.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/construct_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:114)). Its prompt says not to edit, Edit/Write are disabled, and the checkout is read-only ([run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:250), [sandbox](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:816)).\\n- Despite the README saying expectations are controller-only, the one-line public manifest embeds every `expected` answer, and the schema requires it ([manifest.json](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/agentic-tasks-smoke/manifest.json:1), [schema.json](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/agentic-cases/schema.json:5)). The agent sandbox hides it operationally, but the artifact is not a clean public/controller split.\\n- The existing repair pilot provides the right architecture: writable isolated checkouts, exact public issue prompts, hidden future-test overlay only after every agent exits, and base-fails/reference-passes calibration ([README.md](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/agentic-repair-pilot/README.md:11), [controller acceptance](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/run_graph_agentic_repair_pilot.py:1194)). Its acceptance commands are hardcoded for Catch2, Vite, and VS Code, so it is not a generic Multi-SWE oracle ([run_graph_agentic_repair_pilot.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/run_graph_agentic_repair_pilot.py:1068)).\\n\\nRecommended actual-agent design:\\n\\n- One real repair issue per repository, three distinct repositories, selected by a preregistered hash rule from a structurally eligible pool—not by inspecting patches, test outcomes, qrels, or prior system results.\\n- Structural eligibility should require an exact base tree, a public problem statement, a predefined hidden test set, an offline reproducible environment, and controller calibration that fails on base and passes on the reference solution.\\n- Three systems: `file-tools`, `entire-graph`, and `cbm`. All get identical Edit/Write/Bash/test capability; only repository-discovery tooling differs.\\n- Use three fresh repetitions per cell: 3 repos × 3 systems × 3 = 27 attempts. Repetitions estimate stochasticity; they do not increase the repository sample size.\\n- Every attempt gets a fresh base checkout, home, session, product cache/project, and explicit attempt ID. Freeze a balanced rotation such as `ROTATIONS[(repo_index + repetition) % 3]`.\\n- Primary outcome: hidden controller-test acceptance. Patch/reference overlap and agent-selected tests remain diagnostics only.\\n- Run all 27 agents before exposing or executing sealed tests. Preserve operational failures rather than silently retrying.\\n- This must be labeled development-only if it reuses the already-published CORE spike pool or previous repair cases.\\n\\nMinimal frozen artifacts:\\n\\n| File | Required fields |\\n|---|---|\\n| `public-tasks.json` | suite/schema/claim boundary; CORE and Multi-SWE dataset revisions plus source-file hashes; selection rule/seed and `outcome_data_consulted:false`; three opaque case IDs; repo/language/base commit/base tree; exact public prompt and prompt hash; public source-row projection hash |\\n| `sealed-controller/oracles.json` plus content-addressed test blobs | public-manifest hash; per-case source-row hash; hidden test paths/blobs; protected harness paths; argv/cwd/env/timeout for acceptance; dependency/container digest; base-fail/reference-pass calibration commitments; optional reference-patch hash, never patch bytes in the public artifact |\\n| `execution-protocol.json` | hashes of both manifests; three system definitions and binary/source hashes; model/effort/budgets; `repetition_count:3`; explicit 27-attempt schedule; fresh-state/isolation policy; retry policy; runner/scorer hashes; primary metric definition |\\n\\nCurrent blockers:\\n\\n1. No committed Multi-SWE row blobs, row hashes, official problem statements, hidden test patches, acceptance commands, or environment/container bindings.\\n2. The pinned materializations contain base commits/trees and qrel-location mappings, not executable tests. The Graph V8 pinned snapshot artifact also explicitly leaves catalog/rank production unauthorized ([core_bench_development_pinned_snapshots.json](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/graph-v8/core_bench_development_pinned_snapshots.json:1)).\\n3. No outcome-blind structural screen or deterministic three-case selector exists for code-repair eligibility.\\n4. The current smoke keys records only by `(repository, system)`, expects nine records, and has no repetition dimension ([run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/run_agentic_tasks_smoke.py:1228)).\\n5. The Graph spike tool defaults to nonexistent `competitive-eval/core-bench-graph/` paths while the committed inputs are under `core-bench/`; explicit overrides or a path correction are required ([core_bench_graph_spike.py](/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/tools/core_bench_graph_spike.py:25)).\\n\\nI inspected no protected V7 payloads, gold patches, or paid/model outcomes, and made no edits.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/confirmatory_freezer\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/neighbors_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
