{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:09:09.795Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019f75fd-1ba3-7ab1-ba2d-ee2e0dcdb8d5","author":"/root/confirmatory_freezer","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/confirmatory_freezer\nPayload:\nImplemented the identity-safe development cohort freezer and tests:\n\n- `freeze_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py`\n- `test_freeze_agentic_confirmatory_slice.py`\n\nKey behavior:\n\n- Development-only `entire_graph_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke_v1`.\n- Deterministically selects three public CORE-Bench repositories using secret-keyed ranking.\n- Checks every identity-bearing catalog row against the exact Graph V8 HMAC/key contract.\n- Excludes the prior spike, Tasks smoke, oracle overlay, repair-pilot cohort, and supplemental cohorts.\n- Emits only selected repositories and aggregate counts—no matched identities, rank digests, queries, qrels, expectations, scores, or outcomes.\n- Exact default hashes, fail-closed schema/inventory checks, canonical atomic no-overwrite writes, and recomputing validate mode.\n- All execution, paid, repair, scoring, confirmatory, and publication authority flags remain false.\n\nVerification: 32 tests passed, including adjacent V8 exclusion/constructor tests; Ruff and `py_compile` passed.\n\nCaveats:\n\n- The actual protected key was intentionally not used, so no real cohort artifact was generated.\n- The predefined catalog has one ineligible row without a repository identity; it is counted and never selectable. Every identity-bearing row, including ineligible rows, is HMAC-checked.\n- Keyed ranking requires the controller key for reproduction; this intentionally prevents public inference of protected candidates skipped during selection.\n- Repair-run artifacts keep identities opaque, so their known three-repository public cohort is generator-bound in code while all three exact run hashes and the directory inventory are validated.\n- This freezes repositories only. Query selection and sealed CORE qrels require a separate controller-only stage."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
