{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:11:27.836Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba5afd8a0819185c6c43e1525b346","status":"completed","call_id":"call_wFFVUTD5e1NF6ICACK5nq9ZN","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"sed -n '1,220p' competitive-eval/product-optimization-v7/README.md && sed -n '1,220p' competitive-eval/graph-v8/README.md && rg -n 'CORE-Bench|SWE-bench|Multi-SWE|V8|catalog|predefined|agentic' /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/.git/**' | head -320\",\n  workdir: \"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 50000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:11:28.045Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f75ff-37ad-7f02-a027-180070f26b97","call_id":"call_wFFVUTD5e1NF6ICACK5nq9ZN","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Entire Product Optimization V7\n\nV7 is the fresh successor to the scientifically ineligible V6 attempt. V6\ncompleted rank production, but every system failed before retrieval because\nthe frozen sandbox allowed linked-worktree checkout roots without allowing\ntheir external Git administrative directories. The exact failed result remains\nimmutable and cannot support any system claim.\n\n## Burn Boundary\n\n`sem-holdout-burn-v6.json`, SHA-256\n`a91cf1d8c690310584ea69f3543451488dd47eaca50f184080485af67958c479`,\nbinds the exact V6 catalog, screen, manifest, score, result witness, and success\ngates. It requires seed `20260712-sem-confirmatory-v7` and excludes every one\nof the 141 normalized repositories exposed by the V6 candidate catalog. The\nburn artifact contains no repository name, case ID, query, qrel, source path,\nor per-case score.\n\n## Identity-Free Feasibility\n\nBefore any V7 repository identity was ranked or emitted, the aggregate\ncapacity analyzer excluded the baseline, V2, V3, V5, and V6 repository sets\nfrom the frozen SWE-rebench parquet. Capacity artifact\n`sem-aggregate-capacity-v7.json`, SHA-256\n`e10d44657a053a88c045aebfb0c0d845fd4bcb71f40507dcf56d258d907a150a`,\nreports 624 eligible repositories after 981 unique exclusions. Six languages\nremain, but only five have at least two repositories, making the former\nsix-to-seven-language rule structurally infeasible.\n\nThe design selector was fixed before simulation output: retain five languages,\nselect 30 repositories with 4-to-8 per language, test candidate caps\n`24/28/32/36/39`, and choose the strictest large-repository threshold in\n`10/8/6` order followed by the smallest cap with at least 80% modeled joint\nconstruction feasibility. The deterministic 100,000-repetition result is\n`sem-design-capacity-v7.json`, SHA-256\n`210495841f91811a3dc970bfbe2fa9166269a6ab64d9078e606ebb7c9af5da7e`.\nIt selects 36 candidates per language, 180 candidates total, and preserves the\nten-large-repository gate at predicted joint feasibility `0.8212`.\n\nThese artifacts predict construction feasibility only. They contain no V7\nrepository identity, retrieval result, rank, qrel, or quality statistic and do\nnot authorize rank production.\n\n## Immutable Sem Product\n\nEntire Sem PR #23 merged as commit\n`ee416b4e16f4ec3274087347971f8fa9f0f905e4`, preserving the evaluated\ncandidate `7651779199f09745afe585c798aecd0717ecb09b` as its second parent. Both\ncommits have tree `6b0860958084c5202975524dd47923cf02241939`, and their Git diff contains\nzero files.\n\n`sem-product-freeze-v7.json`, SHA-256\n`c6c9a0f6088e4d911b3e4c21cbe1a2775ca5f14f7e06776d413e8d49d62fe9e9`,\nbinds that merge proof to the permanently non-confirmatory development build\nand passing score. It rebuilds the merged tree twice with the exact evaluated\nGo 1.24.13 recipe and version string. Both independent builds reproduce binary\nSHA-256\n`878a89891131a4198dab8fcf20bac4dc4cb6e8910d189dda33786478e6fa4025`.\nThe artifact contains no V7 repository identity, query, judgment, retrieval\nresult, or quality outcome.\n\n## Frozen Retrieval Products and Runtimes\n\n`sem-comparator-products-v7.json`, SHA-256\n`f86634f2c01da5943fa23720cbc03826abecec4a756550d8271e7487c8f7a9fe`,\nfixes the measured retrieval roster to exactly Entire Sem, CBM, BM25, and\nfile-search. Entire Brain remains a coordinated frozen-product prerequisite;\nit is not a fifth Sem retrieval system or comparator.\n\nThe artifact revalidates CBM `0.9.0` at source commit\n`b637e3330c96cfe452da623db068c241aaa3ec01` and binary SHA-256\n`1d118d2f6e72abe7889c520642a1f324802d7818a8351c39e8c5705377ce664e`.\nIt binds the in-process BM25 implementation and configuration, the file-search\nadapter and exact ripgrep package/runtime closure, the comparator runner and\nV6r3 configuration contract, a closed Python standard-library inventory, Git,\nand `/usr/bin/time`. Its freezer SHA-256 is\n`2a4ccb19b4ddeccc038065fb0bc73eb0daea8a197889aa1b46fcfa3af4511c7d`;\nits validator-test SHA-256 is\n`6b3e10b8c1d1be1b3a3f60895de3eb042edb8c81ce6a4367752ddedda5ae5215`.\nThe historical comparator runner's host-environment inheritance is recorded,\nnot accepted: exact V7 runner enforcement remains an unsatisfied blocking\nprerequisite. The identity-free artifact therefore sets both catalog and rank\nauthorization to false.\n\n## Frozen Identity-Free Policy and Schedule\n\n`sem_v7_policies.py` freezes the construction, execution, canary, statistics,\nfailure, publication, and claim policy under semantic SHA-256\n`69b79e03dd540407881e73d2c1c7422166f1dacee5747979c25ffa210c741aa6`.\nThe policy fixes 30 repositories, five languages, six cases per repository,\nthe four native retrieval systems, V6-equivalent native and resource gates,\nrepository-clustered inference, and continued bootstrap/sign-flip RNG streams.\nIt requires normalized-identity exclusion for every prior candidate cohort.\nThe legacy CORE development snapshots, V2 and V6 selected holdouts, and hybrid\ndevelopment pilot are mandatory reconstructible exact-source references with\nfail-closed 1% overlap limits. Baseline, Multi-SWE, V3, and V5 remain explicitly\nidentity-only exclusions where no complete historical source claim is valid.\nThe agent stage is disabled because no model, prompt, provider, or token\ncontract is frozen, so V7 can support only the preregistered native-retrieval\nscope. Both catalog construction and rank production remain unauthorized.\n\n`sem_execution_schedule_v7.py` fixes a deterministic four-system Williams\nschedule, bound to the future manifest and execution-freeze hashes. It accepts\nonly the exact 30-by-6 corpus shape, assigns each system exactly 45 times to\neach position and ordered carryover pair, and binds completed-case resume to\nthe policy's per-case record, independent nonrollback authority ledger,\nnever-rerun, deletion/tamper, retained temporary-evidence, and partial-case\nrerun rules.\nThe module has no persistence or authorization surface. Its source and test\nSHA-256 values are\n`8ab85cb248ac206c354a3c9009df1da5e7f0ecf485db43e22c8cf5de8dac6ead`\nand `6a335b5283ce8d514a5866c43a0cc776699a58c2d931dcb3d58a2551c36479ca`.\n\n## Pre-Catalog Stop\n\nCandidate construction remains prohibited until a separate aggregate boundary\ncommit completes and reviews the remaining work. The product/comparator\nclosure, identity-free policy, and deterministic schedule above are necessary\ninputs, but do not authorize construction by themselves.\n\n1. freeze every screening, materialization, execution, canary, and scoring\n   tool, including all transitive source, test, and runtime bytes;\n2. bind the V6 burn, V7 capacity, V7 design, product, comparator, policy, and\n   schedule hashes in one canonical pre-catalog decision artifact;\n3. require repository disjointness from every prior catalog and from\n   development manifest\n   `b8336d0b7324efc72e559af86151fc500050e865bf9b31bd07b64629132ed1ae`,\n   as required by exclusion witness\n   `e4ce77648319fbd2120008f714a1db4d4bd0c4c3e3ba84662a058f1335722f68`;\n4. persist and revalidate every checkout root, Git directory, and common Git\n   directory in the production sandbox path, and require the active\n   all-checkout in-sandbox probe before execution freeze;\n5. pass the full synthetic failure/resume/publication rehearsal without V7\n   material or quality fields; and\n6. receive independent no-findings review and exact-head CI before the\n   aggregate boundary may authorize mechanical catalog construction only.\n\nIf those gates are not satisfied, V7 must not expose a candidate catalog.\n# Entire Graph V8 pre-catalog evidence\n\nV8 is the fresh-seed successor required by the V7 pre-rank burn. No V8\ncandidate catalog, query, qrel, rank, score, or outcome exists. Catalog,\nranking, scoring, and publication authorization remain false.\n\nThe fresh synthetic execution rehearsal is frozen at\n`graph-synthetic-execution-rehearsal-v8r3.json`, SHA-256\n`8dcc9f1ea5d2fb5715abb74a8781fa7439407cea241cb23065f0bd1fb20c03a5`.\nIt exercised the 180-request, four-system execution path using synthetic data\nonly. Its durable artifact contains aggregate operational evidence and hashes,\nnot retrieval payloads, quality fields, latency/resource values, identities,\nqueries, qrels, ranks, scores, outcomes, or host paths. The artifact is\nstructurally reproducible evidence, not a standalone execution attestation,\nand it authorizes neither catalog construction nor rank production.\n\nThe mandatory prior-source inventories were reconstructed before any V8\ncandidate construction from exact hash-bound public snapshot commitments.\nThey contain only Git source-blob occurrence multisets and aggregate counts;\nthey persist no repository names, paths, queries, qrels, ranks, or outcomes.\n\n| Cohort | Repositories | Snapshots | Occurrences | Unique blobs | Artifact SHA-256 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| CORE development pinned snapshots | 2 | 6 | 84,670 | 35,073 | `e6ede5813bd704448f4eb30b4e606b52e7489f8c0eec111032d1c3ce449470b4` |\n| V2 burned selected cohort | 30 | 177 | 188,154 | 53,827 | `af5c95b5c1119460aaacb28cf9781a5ce589a670d4d7ab3c1fa52058dc2539c6` |\n| V6 selected cohort | 30 | 179 | 113,047 | 44,086 | `fca29b3027d8a025945b86353ed44afa1aaa175274e7e7e3cbd5b8e9b817cc04` |\n| Hybrid development pilot | 12 | 72 | 214,452 | 57,606 | `340375131830c5a9c19be88d508fe58d601925b890eb117ecdc04c17864dd6de` |\n| V7 burned candidate snapshots | 177 | 1,042 | 206,637 | 91,109 | `ff13ac6875542c758b28cd76f676d4061f44c5a2e7b39bd0b30ebd847cacb33b` |\n\nThe freezer is `competitive-eval/tools/freeze_graph_prior_inventories_v8.py`,\nSHA-256 `f67db680d9fe2a2445840f38ad72bd70e41e4f5f5e9888d88ecbff2c437aa160`.\nIt validates every source artifact hash, exact commit resolution, committed\ntrees where available, and the V7 burn/catalog hashes. It deduplicates\nrepository/commit pairs before fetching and emits only after every cohort is\ncomplete and nonempty.\n\nThe 1,221-entry repository exclusion union is HMAC-bound with a protected\n32-byte key. The committed freeze contains no directly enumerable repository\nidentities; construction requires the exact mode-0600 key whose SHA-256 is\nbound in the freeze. The key and the protected V7 catalog are not committed.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-PLAN-2026-07-14.md:35:**Metrics predefined (fixes #5, #6, #9, #10).**\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-PLAN-2026-07-14.md:81:  Analysis per predefined metrics.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/CODEX-RESTART-HANDOVER-2026-07-12.md:78:  review, not a V8 corpus.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/CODEX-RESTART-HANDOVER-2026-07-12.md:95:| `entirehq/brain-bench` | [#16 Add CORE-Bench Level-2 feasibility evaluation](https://github.com/entirehq/brain-bench/pull/16) | `feat/core-bench-spike` at `1b10614a` | `main` | Draft, mergeable, CI green | Maintainer review/merge |\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md:23:frozen-V8 closure failure; fresh CI at the new head was in progress. The 248-attempt Entire Brain schedule still\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md:609:must bind and verify actual producer, catalog, engine, source, and output bytes, then evaluate a larger\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-BENCHMARK-AND-PRODUCT-IMPROVEMENT-GOAL-2026-07-16.md:878:   fixture and actual producer/catalog/engine/source/output bindings. Evaluate packet/admission choices\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:65:| Brain Bench agentic pilot | `/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot` | `codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot` at `d2f13dc15a54b84a954226ab9df76e0086676d99` | clean and pushed | [brain-bench#34](https://github.com/entirehq/brain-bench/pull/34), draft, open, mergeable; fresh CI in progress |\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:204:`codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot` branch at `d2f13dc`, not the ordinary\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:232:`/private/tmp/graph-agentic-tasks-smoke-20260718`. This documentation task did\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:264:Graph V8 still authorizes no catalog, ranking, scoring, or publication.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:275:The failing inherited frozen V8 toolchain closure expects the\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:345:1. Reconcile PR #34’s inherited V8 closure against its base and PR #31; do not\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:355:   keeping Graph V8 catalog/rank/score/publication authority false.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md:428:cd /private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/ENTIRE-BRAIN-RETRIEVAL-RELEVANCE-HANDOVER.md:518:diagnostic-only until real producer/catalog/engine/source evidence is bound. Product-improvement\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/ENTIRE-BRAIN-RETRIEVAL-RELEVANCE-HANDOVER.md:539:  export, authoritative producer/catalog/engine/source bindings, and larger development population\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/ENTIRE-BRAIN-RETRIEVAL-RELEVANCE-HANDOVER.md:652:verify the actual producer, catalog, engine, source, and output bytes before it can change that status.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/handover-top30-eval-2026-06-21.md:123:the fixed-answer semantic and agentic-value scorers in the ranked next work,\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/handover-top30-eval-2026-06-21.md:176:8. Semantic quality and agentic value scoring\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/handover-top30-eval-2026-06-21.md:233:- Semantic quality scoring is still missing, so count-based results are insufficient to prove agentic superiority.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/phase0-semantic-scoring-2026-06-21.md:157:5. Phase 3 (agentic value) STARTED: `tools/score_agentic_value.py` →\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/phase0-semantic-scoring-2026-06-21.md:158:   `results/agentic-value.md`, a deterministic graph-vs-text retrieval-cost proxy\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/competitive-eval-plan.md:14:agentic usefulness.\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/competitive-eval-plan.md:16:Priority order is semantic parity first, then measured agentic value, then\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/competitive-eval-plan.md:37:- Did I claim agentic value without a measured task outcome?\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/ENTIRE-GRAPH-PROVENANCE-2026-07-14.md:57:This record does not authorize V7 cataloging, ranking, scoring, publication,\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/brain-bench-cbm-parity-agentic-plan.md:17:Extend `/Users/thomi/Projects/brain-bench` with a CBM-parity agentic benchmark\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/brain-bench-cbm-parity-agentic-plan.md:23:> Brain-bench includes a CBM-parity agentic benchmark matching the 31-repository\n/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/outdated/2026-07-18/brain-bench-cbm-parity-agentic-plan.md:57:What is miss