{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:26:18.262Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The benchmark contract is now separated into three layers: repository selection reads identity/count metadata only; task materialization reads issue plus patch only for the three selected public repositories; execution binds the product/runtime and preindexes before timing. I’m documenting that boundary now so later code or reviewers cannot quietly collapse setup time, expose gold locations, or relabel this smoke as confirmatory.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:26:18.262Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba92a4720819187cdda641438c2aa","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The benchmark contract is now separated into three layers: repository selection reads identity/count metadata only; task materialization reads issue plus patch only for the three selected public repositories; execution binds the product/runtime and preindexes before timing. I’m documenting that boundary now so later code or reviewers cannot quietly collapse setup time, expose gold locations, or relabel this smoke as confirmatory."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:26:18.281Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5ba92a49508191bec75165a43a57d2","status":"completed","call_id":"call_q875cPm5WyJw8rrbm0B1XVSe","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md\\n+# Entire Graph agentic issue-analysis smoke v1\\n+\\n+This directory defines a three-repository, development-only smoke test of how\\n+an agent investigates a real software-engineering issue. It compares native\\n+file tools, Entire Graph, and Codebase Memory under the same agent runtime,\\n+prompt, checkout, limits, and ordinary file-reading tools. It is intended to\\n+find product defects before a larger preregistered evaluation; it is not a\\n+confirmatory code-repair or broad-superiority result.\\n+\\n+## Frozen source and selection boundary\\n+\\n+Repositories and issues come from the existing `nebius/SWE-rebench-V2` task\\n+set, pinned at dataset revision\\n+`475dd5e8703bb5fb22dd3c60b5d038b019eba1e0`, parquet revision\\n+`550a7d2a8e0ae1a03b393d3974aebbbf1d43fdb4`, and parquet SHA-256\\n+`0e0bf9355f892ad74ae98d4e1c404f39fd6654a8e351ee3e6ab162e4a64cd3ad`.\\n+\\n+The cohort freezer reads only repository identity, language, and source-row\\n+counts. It checks every identity against the protected Graph V8 HMAC exclusion\\n+union and every mandatory public prior cohort before selecting three distinct\\n+languages with a secret-keyed deterministic rule. It emits selected public\\n+repositories and aggregate exclusion counts only. It does not read or emit\\n+issue text, patches, judgments, expected outcomes, ranks, scores, or system\\n+results. This smoke does not change any Graph V8 authorization.\\n+\\n+Only after that cohort is frozen does the materializer read rows belonging to\\n+the three selected public repositories. It deterministically chooses one\\n+structurally eligible issue per repository before any system output exists,\\n+checks out the exact base commit, and validates the resulting Git tree.\\n+\\n+## Agent-visible and controller-only data\\n+\\n+`public-tasks.json` contains the issue prompt and exact base snapshot for each\\n+case. It contains no gold patch, patch-derived path, relevance judgment,\\n+expected answer, rank, score, or outcome.\\n+\\n+`sealed-controller-judgments.json` contains only controller data derived from\\n+the gold patch at the base snapshot. Agents must not receive this file or its\\n+contents. `materialization-attestation.json` binds the cohort, public tasks,\\n+sealed judgments, source, and exact checkouts without granting execution or\\n+publication authority.\\n+\\n+The public problem statement may itself contain solution direction inherited\\n+from the upstream benchmark. Results therefore remain development evidence.\\n+\\n+## Measurement boundary\\n+\\n+Each treatment gets normal targeted file reads. Entire Graph and Codebase\\n+Memory are additional discovery tools in their respective treatments; the\\n+agent chooses how to use them. The protocol does not force a synthetic\\n+search-neighbors-read sequence.\\n+\\n+Entire Graph and Codebase Memory indexing is completed and validated before\\n+any paid agent process or task timer starts. Setup wall time is reported\\n+separately and never charged to task latency. Each repository, repetition, and\\n+treatment receives isolated homes, temporary directories, and product caches.\\n+The immediate smoke has one repetition: three repositories by three systems,\\n+or nine attempts if separately authorized.\\n+\\n+## Current authority\\n+\\n+No model, paid execution, repair, confirmatory use, controller scoring, rank\\n+production, outcome publication, or Graph V8 catalog construction is\\n+authorized merely because these artifacts or tools exist. A paid run requires\\n+a separate exact-hash authorization after all unpaid freeze, materialization,\\n+preindex, and validation gates pass.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:26:21.986Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-2e229eae-7389-4e00-8e59-84dacbd56d9c","turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot/competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Entire Graph agentic issue-analysis smoke v1\n\nThis directory defines a three-repository, development-only smoke test of how\nan agent investigates a real software-engineering issue. It compares native\nfile tools, Entire Graph, and Codebase Memory under the same agent runtime,\nprompt, checkout, limits, and ordinary file-reading tools. It is intended to\nfind product defects before a larger preregistered evaluation; it is not a\nconfirmatory code-repair or broad-superiority result.\n\n## Frozen source and selection boundary\n\nRepositories and issues come from the existing `nebius/SWE-rebench-V2` task\nset, pinned at dataset revision\n`475dd5e8703bb5fb22dd3c60b5d038b019eba1e0`, parquet revision\n`550a7d2a8e0ae1a03b393d3974aebbbf1d43fdb4`, and parquet SHA-256\n`0e0bf9355f892ad74ae98d4e1c404f39fd6654a8e351ee3e6ab162e4a64cd3ad`.\n\nThe cohort freezer reads only repository identity, language, and source-row\ncounts. It checks every identity against the protected Graph V8 HMAC exclusion\nunion and every mandatory public prior cohort before selecting three distinct\nlanguages with a secret-keyed deterministic rule. It emits selected public\nrepositories and aggregate exclusion counts only. It does not read or emit\nissue text, patches, judgments, expected outcomes, ranks, scores, or system\nresults. This smoke does not change any Graph V8 authorization.\n\nOnly after that cohort is frozen does the materializer read rows belonging to\nthe three selected public repositories. It deterministically chooses one\nstructurally eligible issue per repository before any system output exists,\nchecks out the exact base commit, and validates the resulting Git tree.\n\n## Agent-visible and controller-only data\n\n`public-tasks.json` contains the issue prompt and exact base snapshot for each\ncase. It contains no gold patch, patch-derived path, relevance judgment,\nexpected answer, rank, score, or outcome.\n\n`sealed-controller-judgments.json` contains only controller data derived from\nthe gold patch at the base snapshot. Agents must not receive this file or its\ncontents. `materialization-attestation.json` binds the cohort, public tasks,\nsealed judgments, source, and exact checkouts without granting execution or\npublication authority.\n\nThe public problem statement may itself contain solution direction inherited\nfrom the upstream benchmark. Results therefore remain development evidence.\n\n## Measurement boundary\n\nEach treatment gets normal targeted file reads. Entire Graph and Codebase\nMemory are additional discovery tools in their respective treatments; the\nagent chooses how to use them. The protocol does not force a synthetic\nsearch-neighbors-read sequence.\n\nEntire Graph and Codebase Memory indexing is completed and validated before\nany paid agent process or task timer starts. Setup wall time is reported\nseparately and never charged to task latency. Each repository, repetition, and\ntreatment receives isolated homes, temporary directories, and product caches.\nThe immediate smoke has one repetition: three repositories by three systems,\nor nine attempts if separately authorized.\n\n## Current authority\n\nNo model, paid execution, repair, confirmatory use, controller scoring, rank\nproduction, outcome publication, or Graph V8 catalog construction is\nauthorized merely because these artifacts or tools exist. A paid run requires\na separate exact-hash authorization after all unpaid freeze, materialization,\npreindex, and validation gates pass.\n"}},"status":"completed"}}
