{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:35:25.149Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5bab4d28248191a9ea3a9261618068","status":"completed","call_id":"call_WNLGsCeTSfAa3iIjbfAz43ic","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"git diff --no-index /dev/null competitive-eval/tools/materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py | sed -n '1,220p'; git diff --no-index /dev/null competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md | sed -n '1,240p'; wc -l competitive-eval/tools/materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py competitive-eval/tools/test_materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md\",\n  workdir: \"/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 40000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T16:35:25.366Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f7615-2636-74e3-a1ee-b8c54f9024c5","call_id":"call_WNLGsCeTSfAa3iIjbfAz43ic","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"diff --git a/competitive-eval/tools/materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py b/competitive-eval/tools/materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..1050718\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/competitive-eval/tools/materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,1131 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Materialize a sealed, development-only issue-localization smoke.\n+\n+The repository cohort is frozen before this program runs.  This program reads\n+only rows for those three public repositories from the pinned SWE-rebench V2\n+parquet, applies fixed structural eligibility rules, and hash-ranks one case\n+per repository before any product or model output exists.  Agent-visible tasks\n+contain the issue only.  Gold-patch-derived base-snapshot locations are written\n+to a separate controller-only artifact.\n+\n+This program does not run a model, retrieval system, scorer, or repair agent.\n+It grants no confirmatory or publication authority.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import argparse\n+import hashlib\n+import json\n+import re\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+from collections import Counter, defaultdict\n+from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath\n+from typing import Any, Callable, Iterable, Sequence\n+\n+import sem_v7_artifacts as artifacts\n+\n+\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n+SUITE = \"entire_graph_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke_v1\"\n+COHORT_STAGE = \"frozen_unpaid_agentic_issue_analysis_repository_cohort\"\n+PUBLIC_STAGE = \"frozen_public_issue_analysis_tasks\"\n+SEALED_STAGE = \"sealed_controller_issue_localization_judgments\"\n+ATTESTATION_STAGE = \"issue_analysis_materialization_attestation\"\n+CASE_SELECTION_SEED = \"20260718-agentic-issue-analysis-case-v1\"\n+REPOSITORY_COUNT = 3\n+CASES_PER_REPOSITORY = 1\n+\n+DATASET = \"nebius/SWE-rebench-V2\"\n+DATASET_REVISION = \"475dd5e8703bb5fb22dd3c60b5d038b019eba1e0\"\n+PARQUET_REVISION = \"550a7d2a8e0ae1a03b393d3974aebbbf1d43fdb4\"\n+PARQUET_SHA256 = \"0e0bf9355f892ad74ae98d4e1c404f39fd6654a8e351ee3e6ab162e4a64cd3ad\"\n+PARQUET_BYTES = 428_839_266\n+SOURCE_ROW_COUNT = 32_079\n+SOURCE_LOGICAL_PATH = \"data/train-00000-of-00001.parquet\"\n+DATASET_METADATA_SHA256 = (\n+    \"771c15b0983ec7f0884a7bb9652d14b3db6847c274bab5c2c471a67fe84716e3\"\n+)\n+\n+SUITE_DIR = ROOT / \"competitive-eval\" / \"agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1\"\n+DEFAULT_PUBLIC_OUTPUT = SUITE_DIR / \"public-tasks.json\"\n+DEFAULT_SEALED_OUTPUT = SUITE_DIR / \"sealed-controller-judgments.json\"\n+DEFAULT_ATTESTATION_OUTPUT = SUITE_DIR / \"materialization-attestation.json\"\n+DEFAULT_CHECKOUTS_DIR = SUITE_DIR / \"checkouts\"\n+\n+TERM_RE = re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9_./:+-]+\")\n+COMMIT_RE = re.compile(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}\")\n+HUNK_RE = re.compile(r\"^@@ -(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? \\+(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? @@\")\n+MIN_QUERY_TERMS = 3\n+MAX_QUERY_TERMS = 1000\n+MAX_CHANGED_FILES = 8\n+MAX_CHANGED_LINES = 300\n+MAX_REGIONS = 20\n+EXCLUDED_PARTS = {\".git\", \"node_modules\", \"vendor\", \"dist\", \"build\", \"target\"}\n+EXCLUDED_NAMES = {\"package-lock.json\", \"yarn.lock\", \"pnpm-lock.yaml\"}\n+\n+AUTHORITY_FIELDS = (\n+    \"catalog_construction_authorized\",\n+    \"issue_query_construction_authorized\",\n+    \"controller_scoring_authorized\",\n+    \"repair_execution_authorized\",\n+    \"model_execution_authorized\",\n+    \"paid_execution_authorized\",\n+    \"confirmatory_execution_authorized\",\n+    \"confirmatory_use_allowed\",\n+    \"confirmatory_publication_authorized\",\n+    \"rank_production_authorized\",\n+    \"score_production_authorized\",\n+    \"outcome_publication_authorized\",\n+)\n+\n+SOURCE_COLUMNS = (\n+    \"instance_id\",\n+    \"repo\",\n+    \"language\",\n+    \"created_at\",\n+    \"base_commit\",\n+    \"problem_statement\",\n+    \"patch\",\n+)\n+\n+\n+class MaterializationError(ValueError):\n+    \"\"\"Raised when a materialization invariant fails closed.\"\"\"\n+\n+\n+CheckoutProvider = Callable[[Path, dict[str, Any]], dict[str, Any]]\n+\n+\n+def _sha256_json(value: Any) -> str:\n+    return artifacts.sha256_bytes(artifacts.canonical_bytes(value))\n+\n+\n+def _require_string(value: Any, label: str) -> str:\n+    if type(value) is not str or not value.strip():\n+        raise MaterializationError(f\"{label} must be a non-empty string\")\n+    return value.strip()\n+\n+\n+def canonical_repo(value: Any) -> str:\n+    repository = _require_string(value, \"repository identity\")\n+    repository = repository.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\").removesuffix(\".git\").strip(\"/\")\n+    for prefix in (\"https://github.com/\", \"http://github.com/\", \"github.com/\"):\n+        if repository.casefold().startswith(prefix):\n+            repository = repository[len(prefix) :]\n+            break\n+    if repository.casefold().startswith(\"git@github.com:\"):\n+        repository = repository[len(\"git@github.com:\") :]\n+    parts = repository.split(\"/\")\n+    if len(parts) != 2 or any(not part or part in {\".\", \"..\"} for part in parts):\n+        raise MaterializationError(\"repository identity must be GitHub owner/name\")\n+    return \"/\".join(parts)\n+\n+\n+def normalize_repo(value: Any) -> str:\n+    return canonical_repo(value).casefold()\n+\n+\n+def query_terms(query: str) -> list[str]:\n+    return [term.casefold() for term in TERM_RE.findall(query)]\n+\n+\n+def _line_regions(lines: Iterable[int]) -> list[dict[str, int]]:\n+    ordered = sorted(set(lines))\n+    if not ordered:\n+        return []\n+    result: list[dict[str, int]] = []\n+    start = previous = ordered[0]\n+    for line in ordered[1:]:\n+        if line != previous + 1:\n+            result.append({\"start_line\": start, \"end_line\": previous})\n+            start = line\n+        previous = line\n+    result.append({\"start_line\": start, \"end_line\": previous})\n+    return result\n+\n+\n+def patch_judgments(patch: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n+    \"\"\"Project removed old-file lines from a unified diff into base locations.\"\"\"\n+\n+    current_path: str | None = None\n+    old_line = 0\n+    in_hunk = False\n+    changed: dict[str, set[int]] = defaultdict(set)\n+    for line in patch.splitlines():\n+        if line.startswith(\"diff --git \"):\n+            current_path = None\n+            in_hunk = False\n+            continue\n+        if line.startswith(\"--- \"):\n+            raw = line[4:].split(\"\\t\", 1)[0]\n+            current_path = raw[2:] if raw.startswith(\"a/\") else raw\n+            if current_path == \"/dev/null\":\n+                current_path = None\n+            in_hunk = False\n+            continue\n+        match = HUNK_RE.match(line)\n+        if match:\n+            old_line = int(match.group(1))\n+            in_hunk = current_path is not None\n+            continue\n+        if not in_hunk or current_path is None or line.startswith(\"+++\"):\n+            continue\n+        if line.startswith(\"-\") and not line.startswith(\"---\"):\n+            if old_line < 1:\n+                raise MaterializationError(\"patch produced an invalid base line\")\n+            changed[current_path].add(old_line)\n+            old_line += 1\n+        elif line.startswith(\" \"):\n+            old_line += 1\n+        elif line.startswith(\"+\") or line == \"\\\\ No newline at end of file\":\n+            continue\n+        else:\n+            in_hunk = False\n+\n+    judgments: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n+    for path, lines in sorted(changed.items()):\n+        pure = PurePosixPath(path)\n+        folded_parts = {part.casefold() for part in pure.parts}\n+        if (\n+            path.startswith(\"/\")\n+            or \"..\" in pure.parts\n+            or folded_parts & EXCLUDED_PARTS\n+            or pure.name.casefold() in EXCLUDED_NAMES\n+        ):\n+            continue\n+        for region in _line_regions(lines):\n+            judgments.append({\"file_path\": path, **region})\n+    return judgments\n+\n+\n+def _source_projection(row: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, str]:\n+    missing = [field for field in SOURCE_COLUMNS if field not in row]\n+    if missing:\n+        raise MaterializationError(f\"source row is missing fields: {', '.join(missing)}\")\n+    projection = {field: str(row[field]) for field in SOURCE_COLUMNS}\n+    projection[\"repo\"] = canonical_repo(projection[\"repo\"])\n+    projection[\"language\"] = projection[\"language\"].strip().casefold()\n+    projection[\"base_commit\"] = projection[\"base_commit\"].strip().casefold()\n+    for field in SOURCE_COLUMNS:\n+        if not projection[field].strip():\n+            raise MaterializationError(f\"source row {field} is empty\")\n+    if COMMIT_RE.fullmatch(projection[\"base_commit\"]) is None:\ndiff --git a/competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md b/competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..2ca2a19\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@\n+# Entire Graph agentic issue-analysis smoke v1\n+\n+This directory defines a three-repository, development-only smoke test of how\n+an agent investigates a real software-engineering issue. It compares native\n+file tools, Entire Graph, and Codebase Memory under the same agent runtime,\n+prompt, checkout, limits, and ordinary file-reading tools. It is intended to\n+find product defects before a larger preregistered evaluation; it is not a\n+confirmatory code-repair or broad-superiority result.\n+\n+## Frozen source and selection boundary\n+\n+Repositories and issues come from the existing `nebius/SWE-rebench-V2` task\n+set, pinned at dataset revision\n+`475dd5e8703bb5fb22dd3c60b5d038b019eba1e0`, parquet revision\n+`550a7d2a8e0ae1a03b393d3974aebbbf1d43fdb4`, and parquet SHA-256\n+`0e0bf9355f892ad74ae98d4e1c404f39fd6654a8e351ee3e6ab162e4a64cd3ad`.\n+\n+The cohort freezer reads only repository identity, language, and source-row\n+counts. It checks every identity against the protected Graph V8 HMAC exclusion\n+union and every mandatory public prior cohort before selecting three distinct\n+languages with a secret-keyed deterministic rule. It emits selected public\n+repositories and aggregate exclusion counts only. It does not read or emit\n+issue text, patches, judgments, expected outcomes, ranks, scores, or system\n+results. This smoke does not change any Graph V8 authorization.\n+\n+Only after that cohort is frozen does the materializer read rows belonging to\n+the three selected public repositories. It deterministically chooses one\n+structurally eligible issue per repository before any system output exists,\n+checks out the exact base commit, and validates the resulting Git tree.\n+\n+## Agent-visible and controller-only data\n+\n+`public-tasks.json` contains the issue prompt and exact base snapshot for each\n+case. It contains no gold patch, patch-derived path, relevance judgment,\n+expected answer, rank, score, or outcome.\n+\n+`sealed-controller-judgments.json` contains only controller data derived from\n+the gold patch at the base snapshot. Agents must not receive this file or its\n+contents. `materialization-attestation.json` binds the cohort, public tasks,\n+sealed judgments, source, and exact checkouts without granting execution or\n+publication authority.\n+\n+The public problem statement may itself contain solution direction inherited\n+from the upstream benchmark. Results therefore remain development evidence.\n+\n+## Measurement boundary\n+\n+Each treatment gets normal targeted file reads. Entire Graph and Codebase\n+Memory are additional discovery tools in their respective treatments; the\n+agent chooses how to use them. The protocol does not force a synthetic\n+search-neighbors-read sequence.\n+\n+Entire Graph and Codebase Memory indexing is completed and validated before\n+any paid agent process or task timer starts. Setup wall time is reported\n+separately and never charged to task latency. Each repository, repetition, and\n+treatment receives isolated homes, temporary directories, and product caches.\n+The immediate smoke has one repetition: three repositories by three systems,\n+or nine attempts if separately authorized.\n+\n+## Current authority\n+\n+No model, paid execution, repair, confirmatory use, controller scoring, rank\n+production, outcome publication, or Graph V8 catalog construction is\n+authorized merely because these artifacts or tools exist. A paid run requires\n+a separate exact-hash authorization after all unpaid freeze, materialization,\n+preindex, and validation gates pass.\n    1131 competitive-eval/tools/materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py\n     506 competitive-eval/tools/test_materialize_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py\n      66 competitive-eval/agentic-issue-analysis-smoke-v1/README.md\n    1703 total\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
