ing for Claude Opus 4 starts at $15 per million input tokens and $75 per million output tokens, with up to 90% cost savings with prompt caching and 50% cost savings with batch processing. ... We offer a family of Claude models across the spectrum of speed, price, and performance.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModel system cards \\ Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com/system-cards)\nciteturn8search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Claude Opus 4.8  | May 2026  | Read system card\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroducing Claude Sonnet 5 \\ Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-sonnet-5)\nciteturn8search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; Image: Claude Sonnet 5 benchmark table Scores for Sonnet 5 on a variety of evaluations compared to those of Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 4.8 (a more generally capable model, for reference). ... It’s also available in Claude Code and on the Claude Platform, where it launches with introductory pricing of $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens through August 31, 2026, after which it will be priced at $3 per million input tokens and $15 per million output tokens.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPricing \\ Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com/pricing?subjects=claude&type=product)\nciteturn8search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last year; # Pricing ...   * ## Claude Opus 4 ...   * ## Claude Opus 3\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
