{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T17:14:38.948Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The deeper fix has now cut the measured broad warm query from 23.4 seconds to 1.43 seconds while preserving the exhaustive result set and cached health signals. That is a real correction, but I’m not treating 1.43 seconds as the finish line: I’m checking the narrow/no-hit paths and designing a durable query sidecar so preindexed retrieval can avoid rescanning Git objects altogether. The benchmark runner is about 70% complete and still has not made any model or network call.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
