{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T17:24:47.402Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019f7642-58aa-7043-b4dd-571d64d421c8","author":"/root/warm_search_fix","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/warm_search_fix\nPayload:\nImplemented the correctness-preserving warm committed-HEAD search fix.\n\nFiles changed:\n\n- `internal/sem/search.go`\n- `internal/sem/search_cache.go`\n- `internal/sem/search_test.go`\n- `internal/sem/search_cache_test.go`\n- `internal/gitutil/git.go`\n- `internal/gitutil/git_test.go`\n\nKey outcomes:\n\n- Canonical full preindex is reused directly; no query-specific relation re-resolution.\n- Query candidate scope is separate from full graph scope.\n- Committed search uses exact-commit fixed-string Git preselection across all expanded terms with no hidden file cap.\n- Identifier usage discovery uses batched Git postings instead of repository-wide serial reads.\n- Content reads use an exact-commit batch reader.\n- Query and identifier-usage read metrics are disjoint physical reads/bytes.\n- No-hit queries preserve cached completeness and partial failures.\n- Test/docs/generated priors are query-aware and consistently applied.\n- Oversized/minified lexical matches remain searchable; no partial-failure paths are silently dropped.\n- Worktree dirty semantics remain unchanged.\n- Default full-index versus syntax-only-search projection was deliberately not added because it is not semantically exact for C/C++ parsing.\n\nValidation:\n\n- `go test ./internal/gitutil ./internal/sem` passed.\n- `env GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-graph-go-cache mise run check` passed, including race tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\nFresh-preindex measurements on Entire Graph:\n\n- No-hit query: **222 ms**, zero content reads.\n- Narrow realistic query: **1.688 s**, versus **3.151 s** with the frozen old binary.\n- Initial candidate reads fell from 265 files to 31; warm query read 22 MB instead of the repository-wide content pass.\n\nOne measured follow-up optimization is available: raw `git grep -l -z` over the same exact terms took about **100 ms**, versus roughly **1.04 s** for the current `-o -m 1` path-only usage. Switching the tree preselector to a dedicated NUL-delimited path-only API should likely bring the narrow query under one second without changing recall. I did not make that extra edit after the instruction to freeze."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
