{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T17:42:00.581Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019f7652-1c85-7a03-ae6d-b86f8465b725","author":"/root/warm_diff_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/warm_diff_review\nPayload:\n- **P1 — Unbounded cold parsing:** [search.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/internal/sem/search.go:784) returns every grep/path match even with `DisableCache` or no preindex, bypassing `MaxIndexedFiles`. Gate this on a full-cache hit; otherwise cap cold parsing.\n\n- **P1 — Incomplete revision pinning:** [provider.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/internal/sem/provider.go:982) still derives `FILE_CHANGES_WITH` from moving `HEAD`. These history-dependent edges are also stored under a tree-only cache key. Pass the pinned commit to `git log` and key history-derived graphs by commit.\n\n- **P2 — Underreported I/O:** Corpus-wide `git grep` scans in preselection and usage expansion are absent from all new read counters, allowing zero/few reads to be reported after one or two full-tree scans. Add grep scan counters or explicitly rename the fields as Go-process hydration only.\n\n- **P2 — Explicit plural artifact intent ignored:** [search.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph/internal/sem/search.go:2873) checks singular terms while `searchQuerySupplied` ignores derived 0.55 forms. Queries containing `fixtures`, `guides`, `examples`, or `generators` still penalize those requested paths. Track original normalized intent or include plural variants."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
