{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T17:48:05.325Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The local adversarial review found four real Graph issues before commit, and they are being fixed now:\n\n- cold searches could accidentally bypass the documented parse bound;\n- `FILE_CHANGES_WITH` still read moving `HEAD`, making a supposedly pinned graph/cache history-dependent;\n- Git-tree scan work was not explicit in telemetry;\n- plural intent such as “fixtures” or “generators” still received artifact penalties.\n\nThe fixes now gate unbounded hydration on an exact preindex hit, bind history edges/cache keys to the commit, expose Git scan passes/files examined, and handle plural intent. I’m keeping this unpushed until that corrected version is fully green, then it goes up as one reviewed checkpoint.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T17:48:05.325Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5bbc5555bc8191972a50e2b7b00aec","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The local adversarial review found four real Graph issues before commit, and they are being fixed now:\n\n- cold searches could accidentally bypass the documented parse bound;\n- `FILE_CHANGES_WITH` still read moving `HEAD`, making a supposedly pinned graph/cache history-dependent;\n- Git-tree scan work was not explicit in telemetry;\n- plural intent such as “fixtures” or “generators” still received artifact penalties.\n\nThe fixes now gate unbounded hydration on an exact preindex hit, bind history edges/cache keys to the commit, expose Git scan passes/files examined, and handle plural intent. I’m keeping this unpushed until that corrected version is fully green, then it goes up as one reviewed checkpoint."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
