{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T17:54:02.397Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019f765d-201d-7923-892d-2df64b5147e0","author":"/root/runner_security_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/runner_security_review\nPayload:\nActionable findings:\n\n- **P0 — real Claude calls cannot reach Anthropic.** `run_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py:2380-2413` inserts a global `(deny network*)` into the sandbox profile around the Claude process. This denies Claude’s own API transport, not merely tool subprocess traffic. `test_run_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py:1310-1354` asserts the blocker instead of detecting it. **Fix:** separate controller/model transport from sandboxed tool execution; do not globally network-deny the Claude process.\n\n- **P0 — `--bare` makes the copied OAuth credential unusable.** The command adds `--bare` at `:2353-2377`; the current bound Claude binary’s embedded help states that bare mode never reads OAuth/keychain credentials and accepts Anthropic auth only from `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` or an `apiKeyHelper` supplied via `--settings`. The runner nevertheless only copies OAuth `.credentials.json` at `:3271-3283`, while `_agent_environment` at `:2828-2858` supplies neither API-key auth nor helper settings. The test explicitly verifies no API key at `test_run...py:1050,1111`. Thus every real attempt fails authentication even if networking is fixed. **Fix:** use a reviewed isolated API-key/helper transport compatible with bare mode, or remove bare and replace its isolation guarantees explicitly. Add a no-model static capability test against the exact frozen runtime.\n\n- **P1 — credentials and Git/controller-adjacent data are not protected pre-execution.** `Read` is globally auto-allowed and Graph gets wildcard Bash permissions at `:2335-2376`; home/cache paths are sandbox-readable at `:2389-2404`; the OAuth file is placed under that home at `:3274-3283`. `_safe_tool_path`/`_audit_tools` only reject an outside-checkout read or chained/forbidden Bash after the process finishes (`:2475-2696`). A prompt-injected attempt can therefore read the credential or checkout `.git` contents and expose them to the model before the row is marked failed. `.git` is considered safe because it is inside the checkout. The test at `test_run...py:1357-1404` only proves post-hoc classification. **Fix:** enforce path/command policy before tool execution, never place auth material in an agent-readable namespace, exclude `.git` and all non-working-tree paths, and expose Graph through a fixed-argv wrapper rather than wildcard Bash.\n\n- **P1 — valid costs can be rejected, and cache pricing is not exact.** `_usage_and_cost` at `:2699-2720` collapses all cache creation into one counter/rate, ignoring Claude usage’s 5-minute versus 1-hour cache-creation breakdown. `:3070-3078` then requires string-exact equality between that recomputation and JSON `total_cost_usd`. Real result JSON can contain floating artifacts such as `0.7268479999999999`, and 1h cache tokens have a different rate, so valid calls can become `reported_cost_mismatch`. **Fix:** freeze and record TTL-specific counters/rates plus service tier, compute from integer counters, and compare the runtime float only after documented decimal quantization/tolerance.\n\n- **P1 — scoring does not authenticate execution lineage.** `score_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py:595-700` merely checks that `execution_authorization_sha256` is shaped like a hash. Scoring authorization binds only freeze, oracle, results, and scorer hashes at `:988-1003`; `score_authorized` at `:1136-1190` never opens the execution authorization, preflight, run attestation, or per-attempt completion records. A fabricated full-schedule results document can therefore be externally authorized and scored as “real.” The runner creates the missing lineage evidence at `run...py:3396-3415`, but the scorer ignores it. **Fix:** bind and validate exact execution-authorization, preflight, run-attestation, setup, and completion-record hashes before scoring.\n\n- **P1 — the production runner can self-mint paid authorization.** `create_execution_authorization` accepts `paid_execution_authorized=True` at `run...py:1709-1732`, and the public CLI exposes `authorize --paid-execution-authorized` at `:3466-3470`. This defeats the claimed separately reviewed/out-of-band authority boundary; exact hashes only bind what the same command just minted. **Fix:** production code should only emit false authorization; true authorization should be a separately controlled/signed artifact. Keep any true constructor test-only.\n\n- **P2 — retrieval latency may silently become zero.** `_parse_agent_stream` only copies optional `duration_ms`/`elapsed_ms` fields (`:2434-2459`), and `_audit_tools` silently sums whatever is present (`:2649-2691`). Missing durations yield `controller_observed_latency_ms=0` even after retrieval calls, despite the contract calling it controller-observed latency. **Fix:** instrument timing at the controller/tool boundary or fail the attempt when required retrieval durations are absent.\n\n- **P2 — preindexed CBM use is not proven during the task.** Graph cache contents are inventoried before/after, but `run_authorized` only creates `graph_inventory_before` (`:3284-3287`); CBM has neither cache immutability comparison nor cache-hit/readiness telemetry during retrieval. A retrieval can lazily index or mutate its database while still being labeled preindexed. **Fix:** record/verify CBM cache state and product provenance before/after, or make the prepared cache read-only if supported.\n\nNo test invokes a real model: authorized-path tests inject fake credentials/process/sandbox, and the only default-run CLI test fails at the missing-preflight gate. The tests nevertheless mask both P0 blockers."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
