{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:04:41.058Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Root cause confirmed: the test used `:` inside a filename. On Windows that syntax creates an NTFS alternate-data-stream name, so Git never tracked the intended file and the committed-tree search correctly returned nothing. The portable test now uses a valid space-containing filename on Windows while retaining the colon-path assertion on Unix; the focused test and full `internal/gitutil` suite pass locally. I’m committing and pushing that correction now.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
