{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:16:11.955Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019f7671-69b3-77b0-a2c5-43068ae253d2","call_id":"call_wwltRX1STtD9MSShXstU5GMJ","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/neighbors_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/neighbors_review/runtime_research\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only findings; no model/network execution and no edits.\\n\\n- Safe mode/auth: centralize a pure prefix builder returning `[agent, \\\"--bare\\\"]`; build auth status exactly as `[agent, \\\"--bare\\\", \\\"auth\\\", \\\"status\\\", \\\"--json\\\"]`, separate from the paid argv at `run_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py:2335`. Add `auth_probe=None` to `run_authorized` and resolve the default at call time, avoiding an import-time-bound runner. Run it only after both hash gates and isolated auth setup, but before writing the paid-start marker. Require exit 0, JSON object, and `loggedIn is True`; never persist raw auth output. Tests should assert exact argv/order and zero probe calls on every blocked gate.\\n\\n- Auth isolation: hard-denying `.claude/.credentials.json` while Claude itself must read it is impossible in the same sandbox. Add a token loader in `run_graph_agentic_repair_pilot.py:456` and make the legacy copier delegate to it; the smoke can pass the token through `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, leave no auth file, probe it, and scrub it from trusted child environments where possible. Otherwise native `Read` can expose the credential before the post-task audit notices.\\n\\n- Sandbox: `run_agentic_issue_analysis_smoke.py:2406-2413` currently adds `(deny network*)`, which blocks Claude transport. Replace that with outbound allowed/inbound denied; Seatbelt cannot reliably hostname-allowlist CDN-backed model endpoints. The base profile also re-allows the full checkout (`run_graph_agentic_repair_pilot.py:440-443`), including `.git`. Deny `.git` for file-tools and CBM arms, and make `_safe_tool_path` reject it too. Important pitfall: Graph’s `--head` calls likely need `.git`; one shared sandbox cannot deny Claude while granting its Graph child more privilege. That requires a separately privileged broker, or accepting `.git` readability in the Graph arm while removing all native file/shell tools. Update the current sandbox test at lines 1310-1354; its network-denied assertion is now the opposite of viable production behavior.\\n\\n- Fixed-argv Graph: the current `Bash(path search:*)` plus post-hoc parser (`1137-1156`, `2493-2571`) is not a pre-execution security boundary; shell expansion already occurred. A genuinely fixed-argv adapter needs structured inputs and a trusted process constructing `list[str]`. A same-file MCP subcommand is theoretically possible, but not practically small: a child inherits the same `.git` denial, and a controller-started broker adds lifecycle, socket, interpreter/module, sandbox, and attestation bindings. Under a strict no-new-files/small-patch constraint, block the Graph paid arm rather than claim fixed argv.\\n\\n- Cache pricing: preserve top-level `cache_creation_input_tokens`, add normalized nested split counters for `ephemeral_5m_input_tokens` and `ephemeral_1h_input_tokens`, and require their sum to equal the aggregate. Replace the single `cache_creation_input_tokens_usd_per_million` price with separate 5m/1h prices. Update `ATTEMPT_RESULT_SCHEMA`, `PRICE_FIELDS` (`323-328`), `_usage_and_cost` (`2699-2720`), `_zero_usage`, `_prices_from_args`, CLI flags, freeze expectations, and fake result events. Compute `total_model_tokens` from the four top-level counters so split values are not double-counted. Prices remain caller-supplied; do not hardcode unverified current rates.\\n\\n- CBM readiness: reusable primitives already exist at `2020-2059`: exact fixed argv `cbm cli index_status <canonical-project-json>`, normalized `status/project/nodes/error`, and `cache_inventory`. Extract an injectable readiness helper and invoke it after every CBM task, outside task timing, ideally also immediately pre-task to close the preflight/run gap. Require the same project, `indexed`, no error, and node count equal to setup; record a bounded readiness result/hash. Capture inventory before the status probe because the probe itself may touch SQLite. Treat inventory drift separately from readiness unless CBM guarantees byte-stable reads. Current run logic checks only Graph cache mutation (`3284-3342`), so tests need CBM post-probe success, degraded/error, wrong project/nodes, timeout, and no duplicate paid call.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/neighbors_review/scorer_lineage\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
