{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:18:35.850Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The unpaid product preflight is clean on all three frozen repositories:\n\n- Cold full indexing completed in 0.8–1.6s, with zero partial failures. That time is setup-only and will not enter task latency.\n- Reopening the exact caches reports hits at 33ms, 47ms, and 88ms.\n- Warm synthetic validation searches completed internally in 76–189ms and used the exact committed trees.\n\nSo the earlier “file tools are faster because Graph paid indexing during the task” defect is removed in both protocol and observed runtime. I’m now waiting on the secure MCP runner and lineage tests, not on product indexing.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:18:35.850Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5bc37bd19c8191a467c62596904d9d","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The unpaid product preflight is clean on all three frozen repositories:\n\n- Cold full indexing completed in 0.8–1.6s, with zero partial failures. That time is setup-only and will not enter task latency.\n- Reopening the exact caches reports hits at 33ms, 47ms, and 88ms.\n- Warm synthetic validation searches completed internally in 76–189ms and used the exact committed trees.\n\nSo the earlier “file tools are faster because Graph paid indexing during the task” defect is removed in both protocol and observed runtime. I’m now waiting on the secure MCP runner and lineage tests, not on product indexing."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
