{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:18:35.890Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5bc37bd6008191a390370629f88e25","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ntCyq0Jp9blG2RbLSxs8IcaY","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"gh pr view 43 --json title,body,url\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 10000,\n  sandbox_permissions: \"require_escalated\",\n  justification: \"May I inspect PR #43's current description to ensure the exact product changes and verification are documented?\",\n  prefix_rule: [\"gh\", \"pr\", \"view\"]\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:18:36.475Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f7673-9e3a-7dc1-a55e-796a4928f3f9","call_id":"call_ntCyq0Jp9blG2RbLSxs8IcaY","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/1\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- Improves agent search recall with adaptive syntax preselection, sparse lexical regions, reciprocal-rank fusion, focused source windows, and conservative authored/generated mirror deduplication.\\n- Adds `entire graph neighbors` for bounded callers, callees, constructor edges, and compact exact two-hop path families.\\n- Completes general Go, TypeScript/JavaScript, and Python call resolution gaps exposed by repository-disjoint development diagnostics.\\n- Adds `entire graph index`, a durable query-independent HEAD preindex with exact commit/tree/profile/provider provenance, cache-hit telemetry, and repeatable ignore/include scopes.\\n- Lets committed search and neighbor calls prove they consumed the prepared cache; agent output reports the cache state directly.\\n- Preserves cache/cold selective-search parity by rerunning relation resolution over cached parse output, with accurate selective completeness stats.\\n- Keeps positive agent byte budgets bounded and removes generated mirrors from both semantic and deep sparse rankings without merging sibling monorepo packages.\\n\\nThere are no repository-, benchmark-, qrel-, rank-, score-, or outcome-specific product branches.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Exact head: `2c54486fc59b4810c2c2ab8443eb32b9bae6811e`.\\n- `mise run check` passes: format, vet, build, and `go test -race ./...`.\\n- All seven Linux/macOS/Windows GitHub checks pass on the exact head.\\n- Independent Claude Opus review identified cache/default, parity, budget, and mirror-dedup defects; the follow-up commit fixes them with regression coverage.\\n- The earlier Bugbot focused-region-test issue is already fixed: both tests are independent registered Go tests and execute in the full suite.\\n\\nDeterministic replay on the three frozen predefined development repositories, with setup excluded and a fresh cache format:\\n\\n| Repository | Cold full setup | Cached search | Cached neighbors | Useful neighborhood |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\\n| chi | 0.854s | 24ms | 33ms | 1 caller × 6 callees |\\n| Zod | 5.418s | 62ms | 63ms | 7 callers × 2 callees |\\n| Click | 3.090s | 57ms | 94ms | 4 callers × 6 callees |\\n\\nEvery timed retrieval above reported `Index: cache-hit`. Zod includes the real abstract `_parse` target; Click includes the real `_AtomicFile` constructor. Those semantics must be frozen prospectively in any fresh evaluation contract.\\n\\n## Evidence boundary\\n\\nThe previous paid three-repository smoke remains immutable diagnostic evidence, but its wall-time comparison is invalid: Graph and CBM indexing occurred inside the agent timer, Graph was forced through asymmetric duplicate work, CBM was degraded, and attempts competed concurrently. It is not rescored or rewritten here.\\n\\nNo new paid agentic run is included. A broad superiority claim still requires a fresh outcome-blind predefined slice, frozen comparator/product heads, repeated paired attempts, and the corrected preindexed protocol in Brain-Bench PR #34.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nNo Entire Brain changes, V7/V8 catalog/ranking/scoring/publication authorization changes, or benchmark-specific product behavior.\\n\",\"title\":\"Improve agent retrieval and focused graph navigation\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/43\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
