{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:19:16.022Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"I found and am correcting one documentation integrity issue on PR #43: its description still named an “independent Claude Opus review,” but that external review was blocked before disclosure and never occurred. The code was instead reviewed adversarially by local agents. I’m updating the PR to the exact `4e2108c` head, the green 7/7 CI state, and the actual review provenance—no inflated claim stays in the evidence trail.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:19:16.022Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5bc3a3fce08191bfe853688aeef79b","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I found and am correcting one documentation integrity issue on PR #43: its description still named an “independent Claude Opus review,” but that external review was blocked before disclosure and never occurred. The code was instead reviewed adversarially by local agents. I’m updating the PR to the exact `4e2108c` head, the green 7/7 CI state, and the actual review provenance—no inflated claim stays in the evidence trail."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:19:16.054Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5bc3a400208191af9ecd7b9d567909","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6QEZnQqujmBJvZ1NhTMGDMgb","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /private/tmp/entire-graph-pr43-body.md\\n+<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\n+https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/1\\n+<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n+\\n+## What changed\\n+\\n+- Improves agent search recall with adaptive syntax preselection, sparse lexical regions, reciprocal-rank fusion, focused source windows, and conservative authored/generated mirror deduplication.\\n+- Adds `entire graph neighbors` for bounded callers, callees, constructor edges, and compact exact two-hop path families.\\n+- Completes general Go, TypeScript/JavaScript, and Python call resolution gaps exposed by repository-disjoint development diagnostics.\\n+- Adds `entire graph index`, a durable query-independent HEAD preindex with exact commit/tree/profile/provider provenance, cache-hit telemetry, and repeatable ignore/include scopes.\\n+- Adds an exact-commit Git preselection path that reuses the full prepared graph directly, preserves cold/cache parity, and reports honest Git-scan versus Go-hydration telemetry.\\n+- Lets committed search and neighbor calls prove they consumed the prepared cache; agent output reports the cache state directly.\\n+- Keeps positive agent byte budgets bounded and removes generated mirrors from both semantic and deep sparse rankings without merging sibling monorepo packages.\\n+\\n+There are no repository-, benchmark-, qrel-, rank-, score-, or outcome-specific product branches.\\n+\\n+## Validation\\n+\\n+- Exact head: `4e2108c54035fcab6c41bce80404ab674cb308ba`.\\n+- Exact staged runtime SHA-256: `9d4f62ec1e99ddd1ab4a3a9bcd68ab7dbfb98264436e30de21279a85164bd008`; Go build metadata reports the same revision and `vcs.modified=false`.\\n+- `mise run check` passes on the exact head: format, vet, build, and `go test -race ./...`.\\n+- All seven Linux/macOS/Windows GitHub checks pass on the exact head.\\n+- Local adversarial review identified cache/default, parity, budget, mirror-dedup, Unicode preselection, provenance, and telemetry defects; the follow-up commits fix them with regression coverage.\\n+- The Windows-only committed-grep test failure was a portability defect in its colon-containing test filename (an NTFS alternate data stream, not a tracked file). The portable regression now passes without skipping Windows coverage.\\n+- The earlier Bugbot focused-region-test issue is already fixed: both tests are independent registered Go tests and execute in the full suite.\\n+\\n+Deterministic replay on the three frozen predefined development repositories, with setup excluded and a fresh cache format:\\n+\\n+| Repository | Cold full setup | Cached search | Cached neighbors | Useful neighborhood |\\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\\n+| chi | 0.854s | 24ms | 33ms | 1 caller × 6 callees |\\n+| Zod | 5.418s | 62ms | 63ms | 7 callers × 2 callees |\\n+| Click | 3.090s | 57ms | 94ms | 4 callers × 6 callees |\\n+\\n+Every timed retrieval above reported `Index: cache-hit`. Zod includes the real abstract `_parse` target; Click includes the real `_AtomicFile` constructor. Those semantics must be frozen prospectively in any fresh evaluation contract.\\n+\\n+An additional unpaid cache preflight on the newly frozen, repository-disjoint TypeScript/PHP/Java development slice completed full setup with zero partial failures. Reopening the exact caches reported hits in 33–88ms; synthetic warm validation searches completed internally in 76–189ms. Setup remains outside task timing.\\n+\\n+## Evidence boundary\\n+\\n+The previous paid three-repository smoke remains immutable diagnostic evidence, but its wall-time comparison is invalid: Graph and CBM indexing occurred inside the agent timer, Graph was forced through asymmetric duplicate work, CBM was degraded, and attempts competed concurrently. It is not rescored or rewritten here.\\n+\\n+No new paid agentic run is included. A broad superiority claim still requires a fresh outcome-blind predefined slice, frozen comparator/product heads, repeated paired attempts, and the corrected preindexed protocol in Brain-Bench PR #34.\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+No Entire Brain changes, V7/V8 catalog/ranking/scoring/publication authorization changes, or benchmark-specific product behavior.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:19:18.734Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-420199b6-f3b3-4519-ab12-acdbb57243c7","turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /private/tmp/entire-graph-pr43-body.md\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/private/tmp/entire-graph-pr43-body.md":{"type":"add","content":"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/1\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\n## What changed\n\n- Improves agent search recall with adaptive syntax preselection, sparse lexical regions, reciprocal-rank fusion, focused source windows, and conservative authored/generated mirror deduplication.\n- Adds `entire graph neighbors` for bounded callers, callees, constructor edges, and compact exact two-hop path families.\n- Completes general Go, TypeScript/JavaScript, and Python call resolution gaps exposed by repository-disjoint development diagnostics.\n- Adds `entire graph index`, a durable query-independent HEAD preindex with exact commit/tree/profile/provider provenance, cache-hit telemetry, and repeatable ignore/include scopes.\n- Adds an exact-commit Git preselection path that reuses the full prepared graph directly, preserves cold/cache parity, and reports honest Git-scan versus Go-hydration telemetry.\n- Lets committed search and neighbor calls prove they consumed the prepared cache; agent output reports the cache state directly.\n- Keeps positive agent byte budgets bounded and removes generated mirrors from both semantic and deep sparse rankings without merging sibling monorepo packages.\n\nThere are no repository-, benchmark-, qrel-, rank-, score-, or outcome-specific product branches.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Exact head: `4e2108c54035fcab6c41bce80404ab674cb308ba`.\n- Exact staged runtime SHA-256: `9d4f62ec1e99ddd1ab4a3a9bcd68ab7dbfb98264436e30de21279a85164bd008`; Go build metadata reports the same revision and `vcs.modified=false`.\n- `mise run check` passes on the exact head: format, vet, build, and `go test -race ./...`.\n- All seven Linux/macOS/Windows GitHub checks pass on the exact head.\n- Local adversarial review identified cache/default, parity, budget, mirror-dedup, Unicode preselection, provenance, and telemetry defects; the follow-up commits fix them with regression coverage.\n- The Windows-only committed-grep test failure was a portability defect in its colon-containing test filename (an NTFS alternate data stream, not a tracked file). The portable regression now passes without skipping Windows coverage.\n- The earlier Bugbot focused-region-test issue is already fixed: both tests are independent registered Go tests and execute in the full suite.\n\nDeterministic replay on the three frozen predefined development repositories, with setup excluded and a fresh cache format:\n\n| Repository | Cold full setup | Cached search | Cached neighbors | Useful neighborhood |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| chi | 0.854s | 24ms | 33ms | 1 caller × 6 callees |\n| Zod | 5.418s | 62ms | 63ms | 7 callers × 2 callees |\n| Click | 3.090s | 57ms | 94ms | 4 callers × 6 callees |\n\nEvery timed retrieval above reported `Index: cache-hit`. Zod includes the real abstract `_parse` target; Click includes the real `_AtomicFile` constructor. Those semantics must be frozen prospectively in any fresh evaluation contract.\n\nAn additional unpaid cache preflight on the newly frozen, repository-disjoint TypeScript/PHP/Java development slice completed full setup with zero partial failures. Reopening the exact caches reported hits in 33–88ms; synthetic warm validation searches completed internally in 76–189ms. Setup remains outside task timing.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nThe previous paid three-repository smoke remains immutable diagnostic evidence, but its wall-time comparison is invalid: Graph and CBM indexing occurred inside the agent timer, Graph was forced through asymmetric duplicate work, CBM was degraded, and attempts competed concurrently. It is not rescored or rewritten here.\n\nNo new paid agentic run is included. A broad superiority claim still requires a fresh outcome-blind predefined slice, frozen comparator/product heads, repeated paired attempts, and the corrected preindexed protocol in Brain-Bench PR #34.\n\n## Scope\n\nNo Entire Brain changes, V7/V8 catalog/ranking/scoring/publication authorization changes, or benchmark-specific product behavior.\n"}},"status":"completed"}}
