{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:21:13.979Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0bd6d73b974b1fab016a5bc419f1b88191991371c8619b8c7f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_FvuE1ARBpbac9duQyfT97Ttw","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"rg -n -C 5 \\\"Entire Graph|entire-graph|V8|immediate restart objective|superiority|agentic\\\" /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/ENTIRE-BRAIN-AND-BRAIN-BENCH-HANDOVER-2026-07-18.md\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 20000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-18T18:21:14.154Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019f7676-062a-7711-b2a2-e1f21e67070b","call_id":"call_FvuE1ARBpbac9duQyfT97Ttw","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"27-Documents under `outdated/` are provenance only. Do not use their “current,”\n28-“next,” or branch-state wording as present tense.\n29-\n30-### Terminology\n31-\n32:The product formerly named `entire-sem` is now **Entire Graph**, with repository\n33:and current command surface `entire-graph` / `entire graph`. Frozen benchmark\n34-artifacts and exact historical treatment labels retain `entire-sem` where that\n35-was the name actually executed. Renaming an old artifact would break provenance.\n36-\n37-## 2. Terminal goal\n38-\n--\n60-\n61-| Repository / lane | Authoritative checkout | Branch and head | Remote state | Pull request |\n62-|---|---|---|---|---|\n63-| Entire Brain integration | `/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/benchmark-repair-integration/entire-brain` | `codex/benchmark-repair-integration` at `923b8a915925967c8ee1ffab3ff603f688a5427b` | clean and pushed | [entire-brain#75](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/75), draft, open, **conflicting** |\n64-| Entire Brain ordinary checkout | `/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain` | old WIP at `bbe1bdf5` | not the integration candidate | none; do not resume product work here |\n65:| Brain Bench agentic pilot | `/private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot` | `codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot` at `d2f13dc15a54b84a954226ab9df76e0086676d99` | clean and pushed | [brain-bench#34](https://github.com/entirehq/brain-bench/pull/34), draft, open, mergeable; fresh CI in progress |\n66-| Brain Bench ordinary checkout | `/Users/thomi/Projects/brain-bench` | `feat/core-bench-spike` at local `ab07c160696127a537e3ca90e94713b2383f5b7c` | clean but local tracking state is stale; remote branch is `1b10614a10fa8b670f324b607efa3e5f00cd6239` | not the current session lane |\n67:| Entire Graph retrieval candidate | `/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph` | `codex/improve-search-retrieval` at `3928dcc7bffd4c9b16324bd2707e311d5944456d` | clean and pushed | [entire-graph#43](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/43), ready, mergeable, all seven checks green |\n68-\n69-Live remote bases at the handover:\n70-\n71-- Entire Brain `main`: `bc0203b761cbc500bfcb0acff723dad57ae37770`.\n72-- Brain Bench `main`: `da189c95dd94fa18612e268639a2262bd02735c2`.\n73:- Entire Graph `main`: `fafe92878b5e920fe161d8078ee91762fe33e9b4`.\n74-\n75-## 4. Entire Brain integration candidate\n76-\n77-### 4.1 Branch and PR state\n78-\n--\n199-## 6. Brain Bench state\n200-\n201-### 6.1 Current session lane: PR #34\n202-\n203-The session’s Brain Bench work is the clean, pushed\n204:`codex/graph-agentic-repair-pilot` branch at `d2f13dc`, not the ordinary\n205-`feat/core-bench-spike` checkout. It contains 30 commits on top of `89ef74f` and\n206-is stacked on `codex/graph-v7-evidence`.\n207-\n208-PR #34 adds and repairs a three-repository, three-treatment agent-native coding\n209:pilot. It compares native file tools, Entire Graph retrieval, and the full CBM\n210-surface in isolated checkouts, recording edits, tests, transcripts, usage, cost,\n211-timing, and reference-patch alignment. This was a paid/provider-backed\n212-**development pilot using Claude Opus**. It was not a frozen candidate,\n213-private-holdout, or publication-authorized run. Do not conflate it with the\n214-no-provider final Entire Brain A/B described above.\n--\n227-repository and treatment, for nine Claude Opus attempts.\n228-\n229-A separate, pre-existing Codex lane started that live run at 12:36:05 CEST on\n230-2026-07-18 with three workers, model `opus`, 24 turns, a 1,200-second timeout,\n231-and a maximum reported budget of $5 per attempt. Its output directory is\n232:`/private/tmp/graph-agentic-tasks-smoke-20260718`. This documentation task did\n233-not start or authorize it. At this handover checkpoint the process was active\n234-and no completed result set was available. This is development execution, not\n235-Entire Brain confirmatory or holdout execution.\n236-\n237-The new scorer is not ready to support a rankable claim. At `d2f13dc` it branches\n--\n244-\n245-### 6.2 Corrected pilot results\n246-\n247-| Treatment | Eligible acceptance | Raw acceptance |\n248-|---|---:|---:|\n249:| Entire Graph | 1/3 | 1/3 |\n250-| CBM | 1/3 | 1/3 |\n251-| Native file tools | 0/3 | 1/3 |\n252-\n253:Entire Graph used fewer output tokens, tool calls, elapsed time, and reported\n254-cost in this tiny development sample, but it **did not win correctness**. The\n255-later two-case Graph retrieval replay recorded controller acceptance of 0/2.\n256-The VS Code result is a genuine behavioral failure. The Vite repair may be\n257-behaviorally equivalent, but its bound future test calls a reference-only\n258-helper, so that result remains a scorer-validity question rather than an\n259-established behavioral failure. Subsequent retrieval work improved target ranks\n260-in diagnostics only; no later paid replay of those two repair cases was made.\n261-The separate Tasks smoke described above was still running. Three repositories\n262-and a two-case replay are useful for debugging, not for a broad product claim.\n263-\n264:Graph V8 still authorizes no catalog, ranking, scoring, or publication.\n265-\n266-### 6.3 CI state\n267-\n268-The CI run for `d2f13dc` was in progress when this handover was updated. The\n269-immediately preceding run at `fee870b7` was red:\n270-\n271-- 2,331 tests passed;\n272-- 6 tests skipped;\n273-- 1 test failed.\n274-\n275:The failing inherited frozen V8 toolchain closure expects the\n276-`graph_v8_ranking_worker.py` hash prefix `6e80…`, while the inherited current\n277-bytes have prefix `b328…`. PR #31 exhibits the same inherited mismatch. Treat\n278-this as a closure/reconciliation problem unless the fresh run establishes a\n279-different cause. An in-progress rerun is not green evidence.\n280-\n--\n284-`feat/core-bench-spike`, but its upstream view is stale. The live remote branch\n285-head is `1b10614a`; live `main` is `da189c95`. Before reusing this checkout,\n286-fetch explicitly and decide whether the intended work belongs on PR #34 or a\n287-new branch based on current `main`.\n288-\n289:## 7. Entire Graph dependency state\n290-\n291:Entire Graph PR #43 is ready and mergeable at `3928dcc7`; its Linux, macOS, and\n292-Windows builds/tests plus lint are green. It improves coding-agent retrieval via\n293-sparse fusion and causal-neighborhood expansion.\n294-\n295-At that commit, the live capability inventory is:\n296-\n--\n340-The output of this loop is product improvement with benchmark evidence—not more\n341-harness surface for its own sake.\n342-\n343-### Move 3 — close the Brain Bench development branch\n344-\n345:1. Reconcile PR #34’s inherited V8 closure against its base and PR #31; do not\n346-   silently bless new bytes by changing a hash without explaining provenance.\n347-2. Review and fix the replay’s Vite future-test validity and the new smoke\n348-   scorer’s mode-specific and treatment-compliance semantics before another\n349-   paid run.\n350-3. Update the PR description with the corrected 3×3 pilot, the nuanced replay,\n351-   the in-progress/non-rankable Tasks smoke, exact claim boundaries, and current\n352-   test counts.\n353-4. Run the unpaid regression suite and get CI green.\n354-5. Decide whether to land the pilot tooling as development infrastructure while\n355:   keeping Graph V8 catalog/rank/score/publication authority false.\n356-\n357-### Move 4 — complete unpaid benchmark gates\n358-\n359-1. Finish unpaid fixtures and independent review for the new Tasks smoke runner\n360-   and scorer. Quarantine the in-progress raw attempts and do not launch retries\n--\n423-```\n424-\n425-Inspect the Brain Bench pilot:\n426-\n427-```bash\n428:cd /private/tmp/brain-bench-graph-agentic-pilot\n429-git status --short\n430-git fetch origin\n431-gh pr checks 34 --repo entirehq/brain-bench\n432-gh pr view 34 --repo entirehq/brain-bench --web\n433-```\n434-\n435:Inspect the Entire Graph dependency:\n436-\n437-```bash\n438:cd /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\n439-git status --short\n440-git fetch origin\n441:gh pr checks 43 --repo entireio/entire-graph\n442-```\n443-\n444-None of these inspection commands authorizes a paid run, holdout access, branch\n445-integration, or merge.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"5dfd74e8-4c67-4fb7-a4c3-45f47a5e848d"}}}
